ating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 0477bc02 Last Name (required) e7d44315 Email (required) fc139c58 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 40a3965a Last Name (required) 4fbd3a54 Email (required) 8370ffc0 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/hr-manager-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "HR Manager", "description": "HR Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States HR Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode HR Manager Apply Now HR Manager The Provost's office seeks an experienced HR Manager. 522382 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Provost Office Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Manager, Human Resources for the Provost Office is responsible for executing employee personnel actions, leading HR professionals, administering HR policies, and providing strategic recommendations to enhance HR processes. This role involves overseeing daily HR operations, monitoring and advising on staffing plans, and ensuring effective communication and support for the departments that serve the Provost and its constituents. This position provides leadership which includes oversight and management of human resources processes of three staff members. A typical day will consist of leading day-to-day HR operations, overseeing processes and procedures for the multiple units served which include: Strategic support with creation of position descriptions and management of the recruiting process Managing daily HR employee processes including payroll, time and leave, performance management, and answering employee questions Providing onboarding/offboarding As a team leader, this position will monitor and evaluate employee skill development to reach current and future objectives of the team. As such, it is important that the HR Manager be able to instill a customer-focused service attitude within the team while maintaining a collaborative, supportive, and productive environment. The ideal candidate will be able to cultivate professional relationships by understanding departmental nuances to provide credible solutions. They will be an effective communicator who is able to initiate and maintain professional relationships with a diverse group of colleagues. A successful candidate will advocate for the development of people strategies by consulting with other areas of HR on processes related to payroll, benefits, employee relations, compensation, and talent management. About Us The Office of the Provost provides administrative leadership for the university's academic enterprise, driving a culture of academic innovation and excellence in support of our Next-Gen K-State vision and goals. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience in human resources, talent acquisition, or human resource management, including 2 years of supervisory experience of HR professionals in professional office or a shared service environment. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Seven years of relevant experience in higher education in human resources Five to seven years\u2019 experience supervising and leading others Experience supporting strategic HR initiatives and working in complex organizational structures supporting multiple business units PHR or SHRM Certification Experience leading strategic staffing planning and initiatives for a unit Experience with human resources administration and management Experience using an applicant tracking system Experience in higher education Demonstrated ability to handle confidential information Demonstrated ability to promote the organization's mission and vision Ability to initiate and maintain professional relationships with various groups and individuals Ability to communicate effectively and professionally, to work collaboratively and to garner the trust of others. Skilled in conflict resolution Proven ability to think critically and solve complex problems under tight deadlines Additional Role Information: Must be able to become a notary public within 90 days of starting the position. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 9th, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $61,591.00-$85,000.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 89606d86 Last Name (required) 33d307c4 Email (required) 098db959 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 79d90b6c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 97c5925c Last Name (required) 79ac6f9d Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 4931b815 Save N