ce documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 12f1641f Last Name (required) 9a9c9f43 Email (required) a5ef9a2b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 5221aa2f Last Name (required) 8a9eb2c7 Email (required) 681c6025 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/research-technician-manhattan-kansas-united-states-c670e9fa-568e-4c9b-a8bd-01b5dc608187": {"title": "Research Technician", "description": "Research Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Research Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Research Technician Apply Now Research Technician Support plant lipid and Drosophila genetics research through routine lab procedures, including DNA extraction, PCR, sample preparation, and plant/insect care, in Biochemistry and Molecular Biophysics. 522374 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biochem Molecular Biophysics Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 19 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The purpose of this position is to provide reliable technical support for ongoing laboratory research by carrying out routine experimental procedures essential for data generation and project completion. Responsibilities in the Durrett lab include DNA extraction, genotyping, plant growth and maintenance, seed harvesting, and basic lipid analyses, as well as routine laboratory maintenance and support tasks that assist other projects and ensure efficient lab operations. Responsibilities in the Geisbrecht lab include standard molecular biology techniques (DNA extraction, PCR), Drosophila maintenance and husbandry, dissections, and microscopy, in addition to routine laboratory maintenance and support tasks that assist other projects and ensure efficient lab operations. About Us The Department of Biochemistry provides a strong foundation for understanding the molecular basis of biological processes. Our flexible undergraduate and graduate programs prepare students for careers in medicine, agriculture, biotechnology, and other rapidly evolving fields. The department fosters a collaborative community of faculty, graduate assistants (GTAs/GRAs), and students who are committed to research, teaching, and academic excellence. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 High school diploma (or equivalent) Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in biochemistry, biology, or a closely related field \u2022 Experience with lipid analysis techniques \u2022 Demonstrated experience with basic molecular biology techniques, such as DNA extraction, PCR, and related methods \u2022 Experience with plant growth, maintenance, and sample collection in a research setting \u2022 Ability to follow written protocols and standard operating procedures with attention to detail \u2022 Experience recording and organizing experimental data accurately \u2022 Familiarity with basic laboratory safety practices Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Current resume or curriculum vitae Brief cover letter describing relevant experience and interest in the position Contact information for one professional reference Application Window Applications close on: October 19, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $14.90 - $20.11 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5cbfccb7 Last Name (required) 1934622b Email (required) 7962c6bc Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 0eccbca9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 40e656ee Last Name (required) 