Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page. Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 5156fcb9 Last Name (required) 8caa52f1 Email (required) 22237d01 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 1eafcbb5 Last Name (required) 7a33cb42 Email (required) e4147ef6 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/communications-project-manager-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Communications Project Manager", "description": "Communications Project Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Communications Project Manager - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Communications Project Manager Apply Now Communications Project Manager The purpose of the Communications Project Manager is to administer activities associated with the planning and execution of communications, marketing and event projects for the College of Agriculture Dean\u2019s Office. This position will manage project intake, develop creative briefs, establish timelines, coordinate recruitment and stakeholder communication needs, and ensure projects move efficiently from request through completion. The Communications Project Manager will serve as a central point of contact among college leadership, communications staff, campus partners, vendors and contractors while supporting the delivery of high-quality, strategic communications. 522367 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Ag Deans Office & Dir AES Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 25 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The purpose of the Communications Project Manager is to administer activities associated with the planning and execution of communications, marketing and event projects for the College of Agriculture Dean\u2019s Office. This position will manage project intake, develop creative briefs, establish timelines, coordinate recruitment and stakeholder communication needs, and ensure projects move efficiently from request through completion. The Communications Project Manager will serve as a central point of contact among college leadership, communications staff, campus partners, vendors and contractors while supporting the delivery of high-quality, strategic communications. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in a communications-related field. Experience developing and managing project plans, implementation schedules and resource allocations. Experience working in a communications and marketing agency or similar professional communications environment. Knowledge of current agricultural practices and the land grant mission. Experience developing, implementing, and monitoring organizational brand(s) and ensuring branding consistency. Experience with multi-platform communications, including video production and editing; audio production and editing; photography; desktop publishing using the Adobe Creative Suite. Experience with social media tools, web design, blogging platforms, data reporting tools, analytics, keyword searching and search engine optimization (SEO). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on: 10/25/26 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $28.84-$35.38 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f8d8c4fa Last Name (required) b722acc1 Email (required) 5547571a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 36c275e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Agriculture Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Administrative / Professional Agriculture Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 8f3b3896 Last Name (required) 8dd82819 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 41d878dd Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Shar