ey in enhancing security measures, optimizing costs, improving performance, and ensuring end-user satisfaction within the university's IT infrastructure. About Us This role monitors and defends the organization's security posture through real-time analysis, incident response and threat detection. Performs triage of security alerts, executes incident response procedures and conducts threat hunting using security tools. Resolves advanced technical challenges and tunes monitoring systems. May provide guidance and mentoring to other staff and assist in deploying and configuring security technologies. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Telecommunications, or related field. Solid experience in cyber security infrastructure support, focusing on the operational aspects of cyber security protection and detection technologies. Proficiency in applying security technologies, standards, and best practices within an operational context. Practical experience in collaborating with vendors and understanding contractual aspects to support security initiatives. Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively as part of a team and interact with various stakeholders across the organization. Operational Security Implementation: Proven ability to implement strategic initiatives in the realm of infrastructure security, focusing on the practical aspects of deploying security solutions and enhancing the university's defensive capabilities. Cybersecurity Expertise: Solid knowledge of cybersecurity principles, best practices, and frameworks, particularly in applying these to safeguard IT infrastructure and ensure data integrity. Technical Security Proficiency: Practical experience in the technical aspects of security architecture, including the operation and ongoing management of security systems and tools. Budget Awareness for Security Tasks: Understanding of budget considerations in the context of security operations, ensuring efficient use of resources in security tasks and initiatives. Security Technology Application: Skills in applying current and emerging security technologies to meet operational needs, enhancing the university's security posture. Operational Efficiency in Security Services: Ability to contribute to the operational efficiency of the security team, ensuring effective protection across the IT infrastructure. Security Project Participation: Experience in participating in security projects, supporting project management activities, and contributing to the successful completion of security enhancements. Effective Security Communication: Good communication skills, with the ability to convey security concepts and requirements effectively to a variety of audiences. Teamwork in Security Operations: Experience in working collaboratively within the security team and building strong operational relationships to achieve security objectives. Analytical and Operational Problem-Solving: Strong problem-solving skills with a focus on operational challenges in security, capable of identifying and implementing practical solutions. Support in Security Operations and Strategy: Ability to support senior leadership in operationalizing security strategy, providing insights and recommendations for effective security management. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 20, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $80,000-$100,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) b2a2082