ssing unit ensures that all the behind-the-scenes tasks are being completed in an efficient and timely manner. Several aspects of this position involve the application, awarding and administration of federal, state, and institutional aid programs. The incumbent reviews eligibility criteria for the aid programs, awards where appropriate, communicates with applicable individuals, and ensures proper management of the funds is maintained. The Return to Title IV (R2T4) aspects of this position are very complex and time sensitive. Certain functions within the position have mandated timeframes in which tasks must be completed to maintain institutional compliance with Federal Student Aid regulations. Ensuring compliance and following university and office policies and procedures is necessary. About Us The staff members in the Office of Student Financial Assistance serve students and their families at every step of the journey while at Kansas State University to guide students through the scholarship and financial aid process. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma (or equivalent) 3 years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Associates degree or higher 9 or more months work experience in a student financial aid office. 12 or more months work experience performing accounting, budgeting, finance or banking related tasks. Able to research, analyze, interpret, and explain complex regulations and/or policies. Effective verbal and written communication to enhance exemplary customer service skills. Previous work experience utilizing comprehensive student information system or similar technology. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional Reference Application Window Applications close on: October 23,2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 18.04 - $23.00 Hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) e47e1378 Last Name (required) 39373e3d Email (required) 4c5ad6ed Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 50ee0d7e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Student Affairs / Services Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Student Affairs / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) c200e2d4 Last Name (required) 0a01a254 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 2c369b5b Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 131320c1 Last Name (required) 44c757e8 Email (required) 92c5086f Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7b185fff Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager 