tate of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 8d341b25 Last Name (required) 2a019d7d Email (required) beab7098 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) e7576e5f Last Name (required) 1fb213f1 Email (required) 05d46bde Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/hybrid-cloud-engineer-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Hybrid Cloud Engineer", "description": "Hybrid Cloud Engineer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Hybrid Cloud Engineer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Hybrid Cloud Engineer Apply Now Hybrid Cloud Engineer Senior Hybrid Cloud Engineer designs, deploys, and optimizes hybrid cloud infrastructure, using automation and monitoring to improve performance, scalability, security, resource efficiency, and end-user satisfaction. 522339 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site About This Role The Senior Hybrid Cloud Engineer is pivotal in designing, deploying, and managing hybrid cloud solutions to enhance the scalability and performance of the university's IT infrastructure. This position supports the Hybrid Cloud Organization in implementing robust cloud architectures across public and private components, optimizing cloud environments through automation and real-time monitoring. Additionally, the role involves collaborating closely with IT security teams and other IT departments to integrate security measures, manage resources efficiently, and ensure high levels of end-user satisfaction by maintaining a responsive and effective cloud infrastructure. About Us Kansas State University's Division of Information Technology is committed to providing excellent IT services to the K-State community in support of the teaching, learning, research, and service missions. We offer a wide range of information, technology, and communications services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Educational Background: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Cloud Computing, or a related field. Cloud Computing Experience: Solid experience in managing hybrid cloud environments, with a focus on cloud infrastructure design, deployment, and management. Understanding of public and private cloud dynamics is essential. Technical Proficiency: Demonstrated proficiency in using cloud technologies and tools, such as AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, and private cloud solutions. Experience with cloud automation tools, container orchestration (e.g., Kubernetes), and cloud security practices. Collaborative and Vendor Interaction Skills: Proven ability to work effectively within a team, and with cloud service providers and technology vendors. Understanding of the contractual and operational aspects of cloud service agreements and collaborations. Communication Skills: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, capable of effectively conveying complex cloud strategies and configurations to both technical and non-technical stakeholders across the organization. Cloud Infrastructure Implementation: Experience in designing and managing hybrid cloud environments, enhancing scalability and performance. Cloud Security Expertise: Solid knowledge of cloud security principles and best practices, with a focus on safeguarding cloud infrastructures against threats and vulnerabilities. Technical Proficiency in Cloud Technologies: Practical experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) and tools for automation, management, and monitoring. Budget Management for Cloud Projects: Understanding of budget considerations in cloud implementations, ensuring cost-effective allocation and utilization of cloud resources. Advanced Technology Application: Skills in applying both established and emerging cloud technologies to improve cloud infrastructure capabilities. Operational Efficiency in Cloud Services: Demonstrated ability to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of cloud operations, focusing on automation and resource optimization. Cloud Project Participation: Experience in leading and contributing to cloud-based projects, aimed at strategic enhancement of cloud services and integration. Communication Skills in Technology Environments: Excellent communication skills, capable of clearly explaining cloud configurations, strategies, and benefits to both technical and non-technical stakeholders. Team Collaboration in Cloud Implementation: Proven ability to work collaboratively within IT teams, fostering strong relationships to drive cloud adoption and optimization. Analytical and Strategic Problem-Solving: Strong analytical skills with a focus on addressing challenges in cloud environments through innovative solutions. Support in Cloud Strategy and Operations: Ability to support strategic aspects of cloud operations, providing insights and recommendations to optimize cloud infrastructure and services. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $80,000-$95,000 Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 11ba3ac0 Last Name (required) 0a3bb85c Save this job to your favorites or