ne for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 0534d2e2 Last Name (required) 86e03586 Email (required) ffc2de80 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 3ad4a800 Last Name (required) 250c97cf Email (required) 94f7e579 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/vet-nurse-ii-small-animal-emergency-manhattan-kansas-united-states-8092d26d-cd74-4503-b322-a3ae3db35bd5": {"title": "Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency", "description": "Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency Apply Now Vet Nurse II-Small Animal Emergency This position provides veterinary support and performs semi-routine tasks in the Small Animal Emergency Care section of the Veterinary Health Center at Kansas State University. Employee provides assistance in the care of patients through independently performing technical procedures and administering treatments. Other responsibilities include training of students and employees on various tasks, monitoring medical records, and collaboration with colleagues to meet patient care standards. 521477 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Nurse to join our dedicated Small Animal Emergency team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This employee provides assistance in the care of patients through independently performing technical procedures and administering treatments. Other responsibilities include training of students and employees on various tasks, monitoring medical records, and collaboration with colleagues to meet patient care standards. Shifts for this position may vary depending on department needs, however, typical working hours will include Friday and Monday 12am-8am, Saturday and Sunday 12am-12pm. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Option This position is required to be performed on-site . Work is performed on employer premises or designated assignment location. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Completion of a two-year college program in veterinary or animal technology accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA). Two years of relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of basic veterinary medical concepts, animal behavior and animal husbandry. Advanced knowledge of nursing care, service flow, and section requirements. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Ability to perform diagnostic procedures. Ability to work with and provide preventative maintenance for ordinary veterinary medical hospital equipment. Ability to adhere to appropriate safety procedures. Ability to work in high intensity environment. Skilled in time management and prioritizing daily tasks. Skilled in interpersonal communication, written and oral. Skilled in basic computer skills. Ability to train other employees. Be willing to master new techniques. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Contact information for three professional references Application Window Closes October 28, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $22.00-24.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f6e1a8d5 Last Name (required) 6e2ffb53 Email (required) 41ca6aa0 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: e1cd6e46 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 5a40b178 Last Name (required) c185ac05 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later b257d381 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e5843ab4 Last Name (required) 482ccf1d Email (required) 9863e29b Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7240536d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) afb792af Last Name (required) b117cc1c Email (required) 2e662208 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 38c85457 Last Name (required) 38407b03 Email (required) cf3bcd2f Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/food-service-worker-manhattan-kansas-united-states-bf11611b-d8f3-4a25-9e40-9a265975f5a8": {"title": "Food Service Worker", "description": "Food Service Worker - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Food Service Worker - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Food Service Worker Apply Now Food Service Worker Food Service Workers make great food and service happen for K-State students. This benefits eligible position functions as part of a FUN cohesive team providing meals in a Residence Hall Dining facility. Early or late shifts available. 520724 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Food Service Workers are part of a team who make great food and service happen in a large residence hall dining center by providing quality food and service to fun and appreciative students and guests. The 40 hours per week work schedule offers a generous benefits package. The work schedule includes one Saturday or Sunday (one day) every other weekend. A day off will be scheduled either before or after the weekend day. Early and late shifts are available. Duties may include: \u2022 Preparing basic entrees and side dishes using standardized recipes and procedures. \u2022 Setting-up and preparing service platforms, salad bar, fruit/dessert area, and dining room areas for service of food. \u2022 Providing for customer needs during meal service. \u2022 Participating in daily meetings and effectively interacting with others. \u2022 Operating, cleaning, and sanitizing equipment in ware washing area and dish return belts. Cleaning and sanitizing all tableware trays, utensils, pots, pans. \u2022 Cleaning dining facility. \u2022 Laundering, folding, and storing linens. \u2022 May provide training and guidance to hourly student employees. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. As a diverse group, we share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. What a great team to be part of! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Preferred Qualifications: Some knowledge of large scale food preparation, equipment, health sanitation, and safety procedures. Ability to interact with others effectively, harmoniously, and in a courteous, pleasant manner. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to learn to perform basic math computations; to accurately weigh and measure ingredients. Ability to use and care for equipment and handle food safely while preparing high quality products. Commitment to providing high quality services and products. Additional Role Information: Completion of Food Service Training within 6 months of employment. Work regularly requires moderate physical exertion to transport heavy items (up to 50 lbs.) repetitively. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the on-line application. Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 per hour. Some work shifts may be eligible for an additional $.60 per hour shift differential. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 657ba263 Last Name (required) dc646cc6 Email (required) a8de50a8 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4e6184fa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) f30acbdb Last Name (required) 64be081e Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0c9f3d74 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) fe74882b Last Name (required) 11b88fd2 Email (required) 886cf168 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 442493e5 Share Now! Pl