 (required) db042c0a Email (required) 69ad3146 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/event-services-assistant-olathe-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Event Services Assistant", "description": "Event Services Assistant - Olathe, Kansas, United States Event Services Assistant - Olathe, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Event Services Assistant Apply Now Event Services Assistant K-State Olathe (https://olathe.k-state.edu/) seeks an Event Services Assistant to support the Event Manager in delivering professional meetings, conferences, educational programs, and special events at the Kansas State University Olathe Campus. 522324 Olathe, Kansas, United States K-State Olathe Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 18 2026 - 23:55 CDT Hybrid eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role K-State Olathe (https://olathe.k-state.edu/) seeks an Event Services Assistant to support the Event Manager in delivering professional meetings, conferences, educational programs, and special events at the Kansas State University Olathe Campus. The Event Services Assistant coordinates daily event details, room preparations, catering and beverage services, and other event logistics. They maintain accurate reservations and event information in EMS, tracking deadlines and managing approved changes. The Event Services Assistant role provides professional, hospitality-focused communication and support for clients, guests, vendors, and campus partners, and supports on-site event operations while handling routine event needs. About Us Kansas State University Olathe, founded in 2011, is the newest campus in the K-State system and serves Johnson County and the Greater Kansas City region. As a partner in the Johnson County Education and Research Triangle, the campus supports higher education through a unique local investment. K-State Olathe focuses on industry-ready education, professional development, applied research, and regional workforce needs, with programs and partnerships in areas such as food science, animal health, advanced manufacturing, supply chain, community health, and food as medicine. Through academic programs, professional workshops, research facilities, and event space, the campus connects students, professionals, businesses, and community partners to education and innovation that create real-world impact. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid eligible . Hybrid work schedule will be determined in coordination with the supervisor based on operational and business needs. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 A high school diploma (or equivalent) \u2022 One year of relevant experience. \u2022 Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Minimum 2 years of experience in the hospitality industry or equivalent experience. \u2022 Prior experience in food service, catering and/or events. \u2022 Highly detail-oriented with strong organizational skills. \u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office Applications, including Word, Excel, and Publisher. \u2022 Committed to consistently providing a high standard of excellence. \u2022 Maintains a positive, solutions-oriented attitude. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to remain composed under pressure while collaborating effectively with others. \u2022 Ability to independently make decisions surrounding events, with good judgment and discretion. \u2022 Ability to communicate professionally via email, phone, and in-person. \u2022 Ability to juggle multiple events and tasks concurrently. Additional Role Information: \u2022 Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. \u2022 Ability to work a flexible schedule, early mornings, evenings, and weekends as scheduled events require. \u2022 Ability to transport over 40 lbs. Frequent carrying, pushing, and pulling over 40 lbs. \u2022 Ability to stand for prolonged periods of time; ability to walk extensively. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: \u2022 Cover Letter or Letter of Interest \u2022 Resume \u2022 Three (3) Professional References with contact information Incomplete applications will not be considered. Application Window Applications close on: October 18, 2026. Application review will begin on or after the close date. Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.00 - $20.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8e4f1365 Last Name (required) ff0cbd48 Email (required) a2a08a35 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f38d57de Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Event Management / Services Administrative / Professional Event Management / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Olathe, Kansas, United States Olathe, Kansas, United States Worksite Hybrid eligible Hybrid eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save 