egard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside the state of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) b677cfee Last Name (required) 47e78f99 Email (required) e6cd7d79 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) f90bd7a6 Last Name (required) 6e8fc081 Email (required) df808025 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-accounting-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Accounting", "description": "Assistant Professor, Accounting - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor, Accounting - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Accounting Apply Now Assistant Professor, Accounting The Herbel Family School of Accountancy invites applications for a tenure-track position in Accounting at the Assistant Professor level, with an anticipated start date in August of 2027. 522061 Manhattan School of Accountancy Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Nov 1 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Herbel Family School of Accountancy invites applications for a tenure-track position in Accounting at the Assistant Professor level, with an anticipated start date in August of 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels; maintain a productive research agenda targeted toward top-tier accounting journals; provide professional service to the Department, College, and University; and engage in ongoing career development. Candidates from all teaching and research specializations are encouraged to apply. The average teaching load for this position is 2/2; this is equivalent to 4 courses per year (or 2 courses per semester). The ideal candidate will also bring relevant business or professional experience in the accounting industry. The Herbel Family School of Accountancy is a highly collegial academic community with a strong commitment to supporting faculty success through excellence in teaching, meaningful engagement in service, and impactful research. About Us Our goal is to provide excellent undergraduate and graduate degree programs that will prepare students to become successful business professionals in a rapidly evolving and interconnected workplace. The College's comparative advantage derives from a strong, supportive family culture, a talented and well-qualified student population, a faculty committed to high-quality research and teaching, dedicated staff, and strong support from alumni and the business community. Kansas State University offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, retirement plans, and paid time off - vacation, sick and holidays. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.k-state.edu/hr/benefits. Home to Kansas State University, with nearly 22,000 students, Manhattan is a vibrant community of more than 53,000 residents. The university's presence helps create an exceptional quality of life, bringing cultural, educational, and sporting events typically found in much larger metropolitan areas. Known as the \"Little Apple,\" Manhattan offers a lifestyle that feels anything but small. Nestled in the rolling Flint Hills of northeast Kansas, approximately 100 miles west of Kansas City, Manhattan combines the amenities of a thriving city with the warmth and connection of a close-knit university town. Outdoor enthusiasts enjoy easy access to some of Kansas' most beautiful landscapes, including the renowned Konza Prairie and countless opportunities for camping, boating, hunting, fishing, hiking, and biking. Residents also benefit from affordable housing, highly regarded K-12 schools, short commutes, and a crime rate below the national average. Here, you can build a rewarding career without sacrificing the things that matter most. Once you experience the Manhattan way of life, you'll understand why so many people choose to make Manhattan home. For more information about Kansas State University and the College of Business Administration, visit cba.ksu.edu . Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent degree in accounting or a closely related field from an AACSB accredited Business institution. Demonstrated strong potential to conduct high-quality research and publish in leading journals within the accounting discipline. Demonstrated strong potential for high-quality teaching. Ability to contribute to the service mission of the department and college. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Strong research record, demonstrated through publications in leading academic journals and presentations at national and international academic conferences. Prior university-level teaching experience in accounting, with a commitment to student learning and engagement. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Relevant professional work experience that complements academic expertise and enhances teaching and research contributions. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of Application (Cover Letter) explaining why you are interested in this role and how your prior education and experiences prepare you for this role. Resume / Curriculum Vita (CV) Names and Contact Information for 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 1, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 4ccce490 Last Name (required) e6566770 Email (required) bd22ec3b Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f2dfeac3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Education / Instructional Business / Accounting / Finance Education / Instructional Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) cbb6f5da Last Name (required) c346a675 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 31ff1f1e Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) cf49a9dc Last Name (required) 96f14107 Email (required) 820c09a0 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job e0d6b1eb Shar