 Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 9870752f Last Name (required) 9f594795 Email (required) d50b6671 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 03249d62 Last Name (required) af7aa3a0 Email (required) b411cad5 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-iii-info-technology-director-of-enterprise-systems-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems", "description": "Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems Apply Now Director III, Info Technology, Director of Enterprise Systems The Director of Enterprise Systems serves in a management level role, providing strategic and operational direction for the enterprise and administrative application systems. 522277 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Director of Enterprise Systems serves in a management level role, providing strategic and operational direction for the enterprise and administrative application systems. The director will work closely with institutional leadership, senior IT leadership, and representatives of administrative and academic departments to develop and execute the institution\u2019s administrative technology tactical plans. The position provides analysis and recommendations to improve and expand applications, system integrations, and application performance. This position is responsible for the management and implementation of the institution\u2019s ERP (Finance, HR, and Student) systems, CRM, facilities, parking, and other administrative systems. This includes supervision, ongoing training, monitoring system effectiveness, and evaluation for staff supporting these systems. Communication across organizational units within IT, managers, and functional administrators is essential in support of administrative technology planning. About Us Kansas State University's Division of Information Technology is committed to providing excellent IT services to the K-State community in support of the teaching, learning, research, and service missions. We offer a wide range of information, technology, and communications services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and ten years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and five to ten years of experience in higher education enterprise application development, implementation and support. Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution in computer science, information systems, business administration or related field Demonstrated ability to lead a team and effective interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated project management skills, including the ability to effectively deploy resources and manage multiple projects of diverse scopes Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty High level of energy, enthusiasm, and ability to be innovative and creative Effective verbal and written communication skills Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills Detail and results-oriented Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $95,903-$127,072 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 07ed06a6 Last Name (required) 83c59da4 Email (required) 777b6df7 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 33ac3f3b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Computer Science / Information Technology Computer Science / Information Technology Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) fb51bf04 Last Name (required) cd63aa4c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later af7ae699 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e2f747a5 Last Name (required) 1d8b83e8 Email (required) dbf1dab1 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 2082ee3c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapter