s, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 20cf1387 Last Name (required) d6f2ebd9 Email (required) e03ed686 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 088afa8f Last Name (required) e0a10a1a Email (required) 40c71cf8 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/accountant-i-manhattan-kansas-united-states-42375aa2-0f80-41ac-9257-0a22154f0740": {"title": "Accountant I", "description": "Accountant I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Accountant I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Accountant I Apply Now Accountant I Accountant I to perform accounting functions including accounts receivable/payable, reconciliations, budgeting, payments, financial reporting, and program accounting while supporting accurate, timely financial operations. 522308 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Department of Housing and Dining Services (HDS) seeks qualified applicants for an Accountant I to join our financial operations team. This full-time position offers the opportunity to collaborate with others and participate in accounting work critical to the success of a large, complex, self-operated department. HDS is a $50M operation serving more than 4,500 residents. Duties and responsibilities include: \u2022 Manage and track $2.0M non-student accounts receivable process, from invoicing through payment and reconciliation. \u2022 Process and reconcile accounts payable for key revenue generating areas and process interdepartmental transactions. \u2022 Monitor outstanding balances and assist with collection efforts. \u2022 Reconcile revenues, expenses, and account balances across multiple systems. \u2022 Prepare journal entries, reports, and financial records. \u2022 Support budgets and purchasing for student and educational programs. \u2022 Process Dining Dollar redemptions and related vendor payments. \u2022 Process Foundation payments, reimbursements, scholarships, and awards. \u2022 Maintain accurate electronic financial records and documentation. \u2022 Work with university staff, students, vendors, and external organizations. \u2022 Learn and apply university and state financial policies and procedures. About Us The Department of Housing and Dining Services offers award-winning dining centers, residence halls, and apartment neighborhoods. We pride ourselves in taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. Functional areas within the department include administrative, maintenance, student living, and dining services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, accounting, finance or related field Two years accounting/auditing experience or minimum three years in an accounting role requiring familiarity with university, state or federal accounting compliance and GAAP principles, including revenue accrual and reconciliation procedures. Cash handling experience, including auditing cash funds in a retail environment. Experience with PeopleSoft, Oracle, Sap or other similar large ERP financial system. Familiarity with document imaging systems and records retention policies. Ability to interact and communicate effectively with others, including giving direction to student staff and student organization officers. Ability to communicate tactfully when contacting receivables customers with outstanding balances. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Online application Resume Names and contact information for three professional references Letter of interest Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $17.00 - $19.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) a9ff8a62 Last Name (required) e2385656 Email (required) 33a1c419 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 80ede0a7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by 