bilities may include developing or adapting course materials, delivering instruction in online or in-person formats, assessing student learning, providing timely feedback, and maintaining regular communication with students and program faculty. The program is particularly interested in hiring qualified candidates with expertise in investment planning, insurance and risk management, tax planning, and estate planning. Availability of these non-tenure track positions vary and are dependent upon need. Applicants in this pool may or may not be considered. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and placed in a pool for consideration. As positions become available, the program chair will select candidates that meet the program\u2019s instructional needs from the pool and contact those candidates accordingly. About Us The School of Consumer Sciences transforms lives through education, scholarship and community engagement in consumer-focused business disciplines. Through the event and hospitality management, fashion studies, personal financial planning and sensory sciences programs, we prepare learners to live meaningful lives that have a sustainable impact on the well-being of individuals, families and communities. Worksite Description This position is remote eligible , though there may be opportunities for on-campus work depending on instructional needs of the program. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Current CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER\u2122 certification (CFP\u00ae) Professional experience in financial planning or closely related area Master\u2019s degree in financial planning or related field The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Prior college or university teaching experience Ph.D. in financial planning or related field Professional expertise in one or more of the following areas: Investments Insurance Tax planning Estate planning Experience teaching in online learning environments Demonstrated ability to translate professional financial planning experience into applied, student-centered instruction Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter addressing how many courses per semester you may be comfortable teaching and whether you are available to teach in-person Resume or curriculum vitae (CV) Contact information for three professional references Inquiries about the position should be directed to the program chair, Dr. Megan McCoy, at meganmccoy@ksu.edu with the subject line: PFP Instructor Pool. Application Window Applications close on: March 30, 2027 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $5,000 - $6,000 per 3-credit hour course Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 790fa7eb Last Name (required) bace96b3 Email (required) 8b04e4bd Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 835a95c9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Education / Instructional Business / Accounting / Finance Education / Instructional Employment Type Temporary Part-time Temporary Part-time Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite Remote eligible Remote eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it 