t offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 65c1b35d Last Name (required) ba46b1b8 Email (required) 6c5e86bc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) c6dce040 Last Name (required) 230f3e13 Email (required) 190aab7b Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-1863d35d-bfb7-4f43-a2e5-3c73dbfa9597": {"title": "Fellow (Post Doc)", "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) This position is focused on conducting research but may include formal instructional responsibilities. The role includes mentored training for the purpose of further increasing research expertise in a specialized area in order to pursue a specific career path. 522230 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biology Staff Part Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 15 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position is focused on conducting research but may include formal instructional responsibilities. The role includes mentored training for the purpose of further increasing research expertise in a specialized area in order to pursue a specific career path. About Us The Division of Biology at Kansas State University is composed of a dynamic group of tenure-track, research, and instructional faculty, as well as a large number of postdoctoral research associates, graduate students, and support staff. All of these individuals are essential to accomplish the Division of Biology\u2019s mission, to generate and disseminate high-quality biological scientific knowledge through teaching, research, service, and outreach. The research, teaching, and service interests of these individuals, spanning all areas of biological research, teaching and training at the postdoctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels, as well as service and outreach contributions to the broader scientific community and the public. Worksite Description This position is On-site . N/A All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: PhD. The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Valid driver's license. Professional experience working with data and statistical analysis Professional experience working with agencies on applied quantitative problems Statistical experience with an array of quantitative procedures (general and generalized linear model procedures, multivariate analyses, machine learning, specialized visualizations) Knowledge of fish ecology theory, fisheries methods, conservation practice Experience communicating with state and federal decisionmakers Demonstrated knowledge of AI large language models Peer reviewed publications Preferred Qualifications: PhD > 5 years professional experience working with data and statistical analysis > 5 years experience working with agencies on applied quantitative problems Extensive statistical experience with an array of quantitative procedures (general and generalized linear model procedures, multivariate analyses, machine learning, specialized visualizations) Knowledge of fish ecology theory, fisheries methods, conservation practice Extensive experience communicating with state and federal decisionmakers Demonstrated knowledge of AI large language models Substantial record of peer reviewed publications (> 20) Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Contact information for three references Application Window Applications close on:October 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $41,995.20 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ade52a56 Last Name (required) 1726d675 Email (required) 20e60528 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 117e3b3c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Part Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Part Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) e259fdac Last Name (required) 82615def Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later b8e90426 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) d67aba9e Last Name (required) 67d7982f Email (required) 5d7d69c3 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job db669ef0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color 