 by utilizing shipping software, handheld scanners, and various computer programs. About Us This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting campus and federal mail from various campus locations. Worksite Description This position is On-site . Employee in this position is allowed considerable latitude in completing all work assignments. Instructions are given verbally and in writing. United States Postal Service manuals, United Parcel Service manuals, charts, and bulletins are provided and updated regularly. Assignments are given verbally and in writing. Very particular attention is given to detail. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer high school graduate or equivalent and two years\u2019 experience in a major mail room operation. Prefer knowledge of United States Postal Service and United Parcel Service regulations, rapid reading ability and memorization skills for sorting of mail, and data entry ability. Additional Role Information: This position exists to provide mail service to the campus community by sorting, delivering, and collecting campus and federal mail from various campus locations. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume (3) Professional References Application Window Applications close on: 10-30-2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $ 13.22 - 19.82 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 1c0dc314 Last N