ted. 522266 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an Animal Technician I to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position supports the routine and specialized care of hospitalized animals in the VHC by maintaining and ensuring a sanitary and safe environment for patients, faculty, staff, students, and visitors. This position is primarily responsible for the cleaning and disinfecting of small animal common and ancillary areas of the hospital. Working hours for this position will be Sunday-Thursday, 8am-5pm with occasional on-call coverage on weekends and holidays. Individuals in this position must be self-motivated and detail-oriented. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Some positions may require additional education (or relevant experience) that will be specified on the position description. Various training and/or certification may be required. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with companion animals/exotics. 1 year of relevant experience. High school diploma. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close: 10/16/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.50-$17.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 1c2281ee Last Name (required) 1abac63d Email (required) 26cf3ffa Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 95eda827 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 1fe8d355 Last Name (required) dad37d7c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 62602382 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 8a635859 Last Name (required) 2778e3a8 Email (required) abb3d50b Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 466f61ef Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashieri