o practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) f1143dab Last Name (required) 77fbeff8 Email (required) ce4d0dca Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) fc9d01e0 Last Name (required) 49f169bf Email (required) ba91f59d Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-in-regional-community-planning-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Regional & Community Planning", "description": "Assistant Professor in Regional & Community Planning - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor in Regional & Community Planning - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor in Regional & Community Planning Apply Now Assistant Professor in Regional & Community Planning The Department of Landscape Architecture and Regional & Community Planning (LARCP) at Kansas State University (K-State) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position in Regional and Community Planning. 522172 Manhattan Landscape Arch Reg & Comm Plan Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Jan 8 2027 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role We are seeking qualified candidates from all areas of planning. Ideal candidates will have teaching, research, and/or practical experience in urban design and development, planning theory, qualitative methods and/or community engagement. Successful candidate will teach courses in our Regional & Community Planning, Real Estate and Community Development, and Community Development programs. As a member of the LARCP faculty, the successful candidate will: \u2022 Deliver creative, effective teaching in core curricula and area of expertise \u2022 Engage in significant, peer-reviewed research, scholarship, and/or creative activities \u2022 Supervise independent graduate research \u2022 Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service \u2022 Contribute to an environment that fosters collegiality internally and externally through interdisciplinary collaboration About Us The Department of Landscape Architecture and Regional & Community Planning (LARCP) is in the College of Architecture, Planning and Design (APDesign) at Kansas State University (K-State), a land grant institution located in Manhattan, KS. APDesign is an interdisciplinary design college with top-ranked and accredited professional planning and design programs situated in Seaton/Regnier Complex, a world-class facility in the heart of campus. The department offers accredited master\u2019s degrees in Regional & Community Planning and Landscape Architecture through five-year non-baccalaureate and traditional post-baccalaureate tracks. The department also offers a bachelor\u2019s degree in Real Estate and Community Development and an online master\u2019s degree in Community Development, as well as an undergraduate certificate and minor in Community Planning and a graduate certificate in Community Development. In addition, APDesign offers an interdisciplinary Ph.D. degree in Environmental Design & Planning. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 Ph.D. in Planning or a closely allied field or show evidence that a Ph.D. will be completed prior to the start of the appointment \u2022 Demonstrated evidence of or potential for inspired teaching \u2022 Demonstrated evidence of or potential for scholarly productivity \u2022 Ability to help students develop career-ready professional skills \u2022 Ability to work with a wide range of student interests and academic levels The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Ability to expand existing program faculty expertise and grow the department in new areas \u2022 A degree in Planning or Community Development \u2022 Experience with community-engaged research or service-learning projects \u2022 Relevant professional experience Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Letter of interest with a clear statement of how you meet the minimum and preferred qualifications 2. Curriculum vitae 3. A teaching statement outlining prior teaching experience, teaching approach, and future teaching interests (1-2 pages) 4. Names of three references (including title, relationship to candidate, mailing address, telephone number, and email address) Application Window Applications close on January 8, 2027 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 67026bd7 Last Name (required) 3c02a595 Email (required) 2f6f4716 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 15deca43 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Architecture / Construction / Design Architecture / Construction / Design Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) f3a97e41 Last Name (required) 46643905 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 23711f9b Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 66583daa Last Name (required) 43bd59fa Email (required) eaab0616 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 11d9c1f0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Aut