tions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/diagnostic-technician-i-or-ii-bacteriology-manhattan-kansas-united-states-40b4f8d7-3679-4153-8a75-48bbc9659e6b": {"title": "Diagnostic Technician I or II \u2013 Bacteriology", "description": "Diagnostic Technician I or II \u2013 Bacteriology - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Diagnostic Technician I or II \u2013 Bacteriology - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Diagnostic Technician I or II \u2013 Bacteriology Apply Now Diagnostic Technician I or II \u2013 Bacteriology This position exists to process diagnostic specimens and utilize selective media preparations to enhance the isolation and identification of pathogenic bacteria and to conduct antibacterial sensitivity testing. This employee will assist the laboratory supervisor and other collect faculty in ongoing research projects by isolating and selecting pure colonies of bacteria for identification and pathogenicity studies and refer to reference laboratories where appropriate. The person in this position analyzes this information and translates it into a report for our clients. 521722 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Diagnostic Lab Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 31 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to process diagnostic specimens and utilize selective media preparations to enhance the isolation and identification of pathogenic bacteria and to conduct antibacterial sensitivity testing. This employee will assist the laboratory supervisor and other collect faculty in ongoing research projects by isolating and selecting pure colonies of bacteria for identification and pathogenicity studies and refer to reference laboratories where appropriate. The person in this position analyzes this information and translates it into a report for our clients. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Diagnostic Technician I - Requires a high school diploma and two years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Diagnostic Technician II - Requires an associate degree and two years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: One year experience with diagnostic microbiology Experience in veterinary diagnostic setting preferred Ability to work well with people Ability to work weekends as needed Ability to know the differences in pathogenic vs. non-pathogenic bacterial growth Computer skills and ability to use a database software package Knowledge of handling pathogens Organization and communication skills Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: 10/31/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.76 - $28.49 per hour Hiring manager will determine appropriate position level candidates will be hired into based on candidate education, experience, and department needs. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) cf1eabdc Last Name (required) d83bb624 Email (required) bd2ed7ca Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 9a64d0fd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) ecafc3b5 Last Name (required) 5c78e030 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 84512a77 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 34cb813f Last Name (required) 5b25f4a2 Email (required) b4410f28 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0dda41b3 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Sem