 the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/program-assistant-manhattan-kansas-united-states-a3238dbd-d62b-46d1-8f92-8b3edbdc8a7f": {"title": "Program Assistant", "description": "Program Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Program Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Program Assistant Apply Now Program Assistant Join K-State Extension's 4-H Youth Development team! This position supports statewide 4-H programs through administrative, systems, and logistical support that helps deliver high-quality experiences for youth, families, and communities across Kansas. 522249 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Extension Programs Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site About This Role This position will assist 4-H Specialists and Program Coordinators in giving reliable, timely, and accurate information through systems and logistical support to statewide processes. Provide customer service to local extension units, university partnerships, program participants and families on a daily basis. Responsible for moving interested persons through the online volunteer screening processes and invoicing to local extension units, financials, logistics for select 4-H events, online enrollment management support, general office processes and other administrative support. About Us K-State Extension improves the lives, livelihoods, and communities of Kansans through education, research, engagement, and leadership. Serving all 105 counties, we connect university research with practical solutions that strengthen agriculture, natural resources, youth development, health, economic vitality, and communities across Kansas. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated customer service skills Strong verbal and written communication skills Three years of administrative assistance experience Experience with on-line enrollment systems Experience with data collections systems (ie., Qualtrics) Familiarity with 4-H Youth Development programs Knowledge of K-State Extension Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Resume Three professional references Application Window Applications close on: October 16, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.36 - $20.44 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) d49e4d23 Last Name (required) 419915a7 Email (required) ea87b05a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 0b65da39 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Extension Agent / Educator Administrative / Professional Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Extension Agent / Educator Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) af87bfd3 Last Name (required) 794a236b Save this 