": "Physician", "description": "Physician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Physician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Physician Apply Now Physician Lafene Health Center is looking for a highly dedicated and enthusiastic Sports Medicine Physician. 522232 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Lafene Student Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Oct 16 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position directly provides exceptional sports medicine and family practice healthcare services to eligible patients at Lafene Health Center and remote campus locations. The doctor will maintain a scope of practice contemporary to the needs of college health including diagnosis, treatment, and referral for consultation or specialty services, follow-up care, and serve as a positive and respectful resource to patients. Works cooperatively with the Lafene Health Center\u2019s Medical Director, Administration, and all clinical and clerical staff in order to maintain a harmonious and productive work environment to the benefit of our patients. Works cooperatively with other Kansas State University departments to be a sports medicine and healthcare resource, as well as to provide care consistent with appropriate standards for sports medicine. Collaborating departments may include the K-State Athletics, Inc., Recreational Services, Department of Food, Nutrition, Dietetics and Health, etc. Provides clinical expertise in support of continuous quality initiatives, focused quality improvements and accreditation standards for Lafene Health Center. Other duties as assigned. About Us Lafene Health Center provides students with accessible, high-quality, and affordable outpatient healthcare, focusing on keeping students healthy and promoting a healthy campus community. Care is provided by board-certified physicians, nurse practitioners, and nursing professionals, ensuring students receive the same high-quality care they would expect from their healthcare providers at home. Students have access to coordinated and comprehensive services designed to build and maintain their overall well-being. We believe that good health is essential for academic success. The mission of Lafene Health Center at Kansas State University is to offer accessible, high-quality, affordable outpatient healthcare services on the Manhattan campus while also providing exceptional health and well-being education to the student body and the larger Kansas State University community. This mission is guided by the Health Center's core values of compassion, mutual respect, adherence to evidence-based healthcare and university standards, appreciation for timeliness, and collaboration, which ensures students receive respectful, efficient, and comprehensive care while fostering the best possible healthcare experience. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a doctorate degree in medicine and one year of relevant experience. Must be eligible to obtain a license to practice medicine in the state of Kansas. This position requires advanced medical knowledge and clinical training, which are most reliably developed through a doctorate in medicine\u2014a prerequisite for medical licensure. Combined with at least one year of relevant experience, these qualifications ensure the candidate is prepared to deliver high-quality patient care, develop treatment plans, and collaborate effectively with medical staff. Preferred Qualifications: Treatment of sports related and/or musculoskeletal injuries and conditions. Board certified in Sports Medicine. Additional Role Information: Variable hours during evenings and weekends to provide coverage for athletic events and practices. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: October 16, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $200,000.00 - $215,000.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) bd4cf8c9 Last Name (required) 0d1c20c4 Email (required) 069939ef Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 727e9b7a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health Profession Health Profession Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 257e7928 Last Name (required) 7509e1e6 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later f2023cd0 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 2560e637 Last Name (required) b8efefff Email (required) ebbccdf3 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 660d1d6c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remain