ional oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) a58c666d Last Name (required) 06b6d31d Email (required) 3396d0d6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) f0ef61c2 Last Name (required) 1f8f4901 Email (required) 3d36fe84 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/dean-of-the-graduate-school-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Dean of the Graduate School", "description": "Dean of the Graduate School - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Dean of the Graduate School - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Dean of the Graduate School Dean of the Graduate School Kansas State University and ACES seek a Dean of the Graduate School. 522196 Manhattan, Kansas Dean of Graduate School Academic / Faculty - 12 month Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Dean of the Graduate School will assume this role during an exciting time as the university advances innovative graduate program and strategic enrollment efforts. This is an extraordinary opportunity for a dynamic, outward facing, student-focused leader to serve as the Dean of the Graduate School within a public R1, land-grant university. The Dean will work closely with the president, provost, deans, vice provosts, vice president for research, and other senior leaders to formulate and implement a comprehensive and visionary strategy that engages prospective and current graduate students from Kansas, across the country, and internationally. As a dynamic leader, the Dean will ensure the growth, development, quality, and continuation of graduate programs and graduate education at K-State, providing strategic leadership and vision to advance graduate education in directions consistent with the Next Gen K-State Strategic Plan . The Dean will work collaboratively with partners across the three physical campuses and within nine colleges to develop an integrated, analytically informed, and collaborative approach to graduate program enrollment. This role requires an ability to advance K-State\u2019s graduate programs with a fresh, relevant perspective. The Dean of the Graduate School provides academic, curricular, policy, research, enrollment, strategic, and administrative leadership on matters related to graduate education at K-State. The Dean cultivates progressive academic and administrative policies related to graduate education, oversees the operations of the Graduate School, and fosters collaborative relationships with faculty, program coordinators, deans, administrators, students, and other Graduate School stakeholders. The Dean ensures plans, policies, practices, procedures, and programs align with university-wide and college-level strategic directions. The position reports directly to the Provost and Executive Vice President, Jesse Perez Mendez , and serves as a member of the Academic Leadership Council and Deans Council. To learn more about the opportunity and the Manhattan community, please view our executive profile . For information on how to apply or to submit nominations, please refer to the Search Process section at the end of this document. About Us Since 1868, the Kansas State University Graduate School has prepared students for advanced careers in research, scholarship and professional practice. Today, K-State serves about 4,200 graduate students across 200 graduate degree and certificate programs, with 57% of graduate students coming from outside Kansas. Graduate programs are offered across three campuses, with more than 70 graduate programs available online and more than 80 accelerated bachelor\u2019s/master\u2019s degree programs. Another 500 DVM students are enrolled in K-State\u2019s College of Veterinary Medicine. The Graduate School works across the University to advance innovative graduate programs, strengthen academic and professional preparation, support graduate students and faculty, and foster research addressing complex challenges. Its mission emphasizes a graduate education culture responsive to an evolving economy and connected to communities at the local, state, regional and international levels. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or terminal professional degree from an accredited university and qualifications as an accomplished scholar and educator that satisfies the requirements for the rank of professor in one of the university\u2019s academic departments. Record of success as an academic administrator in higher education with relevant administrative and managerial experience, including development and stewardship of fiscal and human resources, and experience overseeing graduate programs. Proven leadership with the demonstrated ability to work effectively with university senior leadership, faculty, and students to craft a strategic vision for graduate programs and enrollment management, engage stakeholders in implementation, and build collaborative relationships across the university. Strategic and creative planner with demonstrated organizational, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. Demonstrated a deep understanding of the complexities of graduate enrollment management and demonstrated experience with best enrollment practices, including in the areas of domestic and international student recruitment, admissions, and financial aid. Deep understanding of graduate education trends and efforts nationally and internationally and of the challenges and issues facing higher education. Excellent oral and written communication skills with a demonstrated ability to articulate matters of complexity and nuance to multiple and varied groups of stakeholders. Demonstrated dedication to student and faculty services with a successful record supporting and advocating for graduate students. Proven ability to initiate, lead, and facilitate change; adapt to changing conditions; and navigate the complexity and ambiguity of a large public university. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated record of innovation and accomplishment in graduate education at a major research university. Firm grasp of the opportunities and advantages of a land-grant university and R1 status. History of grant funding and research innovation. Data savvy with proven ability to utilize data in the analysis of decision-making and operations and experience implementing new technologies to support operations. Demonstrated success in external fundraising and philanthropy. Active involvement in the Council of Graduate Schools (CGS). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship Search Process For full consideration, please apply by October 21, 2026 To be viewed by the search firm, you must apply directly at: https://acesrch.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a21esjyxxnir Please apply through the application link and do not email applications. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and should include a cover letter and curriculum vita. Ideally, cover letters should not exceed two pages. All applications are treated confidentially. Inquiries, referrals and nominations are also treated confidentially. Inquiries and questions: Please send to KStateDeanGrad@acesrch.com Nominations and referrals: Please send the nominee\u2019s name, title and contact information, if available, to nominations@acesrch.com Application Window Applications close on: October 21st, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 12f73629 Last Name (required) 607f8d3c Email (required) 1af215e4 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 6645935c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education / Instructional Executive / Director / Management Education / Instructional Executive / Director / Management Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 12 month Academic / Faculty - 12 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 0f98baa3 Last Name (required) 37163bce Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 23a913f2 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 5b2b91f0 Last Name (required) 8d4745fc Email (required) b7d77b80 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 787b0e04 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 94e6c26f Last Name (required) 4aacc6bb Email (required) 658e2cdd Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-communication-sciences-disorders-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Communication Sciences & Disorders", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Communication Sciences & Disorders - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor, Communication Sciences & Disorders - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor, Communication Sciences & Disorders Apply Now Assistant or Associate Professor, Communication Sciences & Disorders The School of Health Sciences, within the College of Health and Human Sciences, is looking to hire two 9-month faculty members at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (tenure-track) to join their Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD) program. 522150 Manhattan School of Health Sciences Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The School of Health Sciences, within the College of Health and Human Sciences, is looking to hire two 9-month faculty members at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (tenure-track) to join their Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD) program. We welcome candidates with expertise in any area of speech-language pathology, although candidates with a background in dysphagia, adult neurogenic communication disorders, and/or neuroanatomy are especially encouraged to apply, as these areas align with current curriculum priorities. Successful candidates will join a program with an active interprofessional education initiative, an on-campus speech and hearing clinic, strong connections to the local healthcare and education communities, and a school-level commitment to translational and community-engaged scholarship. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to : Establish and maintain an active, externally funded program of research, with dissemination through peer-reviewed outlets Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses aligned with area/s of expertise and program need Advise graduate students Provide service to the program, school, college, and university Engage in interdisciplinary and collaborative scholarship opportunities within the school The selected candidates will be expected to maintain a 2:2 teaching load across the academic year, equivalent to 0.4 FTE, with allocation of remaining tenths related to research and service being negotiable. These 9-month positions at the rank of assistant or associate professor have a preferred starting date of August 2027 , with a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Spring or summer 2027 start dates may be possible upon request. Individuals with a clinical doctorate may be considered for a non-tenure track faculty position. For more information, please reach out to Dr. Bob Garcia at rgarcia@ksu.edu . About Us The Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD) program has been a nationally recognized presence at Kansas State University for more than 50 years and is consistently ranked in the top 25% of CSD programs nationally by U.S. News & World Report. The program offers a rigorous, accredited Master of Science in Communication Sciences and Disorders alongside a pre-professional undergraduate major, serving students across the Midwest and beyond. The K-State Speech and Hearing Center, located on campus, provides a rich applied research and clinical training environment with access to a varied community caseload across communication and swallowing disorders. The Center serves as a hub for faculty-student collaborative scholarship and direct interprofessional education opportunities. The CSD program is housed within the School of Health Sciences, which includes programs such as Athletic Training, Dietetics, Food and Nutrition, Kinesiology, Physician Assistant, and Public Health. This multi-disciplinary structure creates frequent opportunities for interprofessional education and collaborative research. The College of Health and Human Sciences inspires and prepares passionate and caring individuals for a meaningful life and career that promotes human well-being in the areas of consumer sciences, health sciences, and human sciences. Home to 16 undergraduate and 22 graduate programs, we provide students with the education and skills needed to make an impact on the lives of individuals, families, and communities. For more information, visit https://www.hhs.k-state.edu/ . Kansas State University is a distinguished public, land-grant institution renowned for the excellence of its faculty, students, staff, academic programs, research, and service. The university has an enrollment of more than 22,200 students from all 50 states and more than 100 countries. K-State was recognized by the Princeton Review as one of America\u2019s best colleges, and U.S. News & World Report lists the university among the top 75 public universities in the U.S. K-State is centered on a 664-acre campus in Manhattan, located 50 miles west of the state capital of Topeka and 125 miles west of Kansas City in the rolling Flint Hills. Manhattan, nicknamed the \u201cLittle Apple,\u201d provides access to a wide range of educational, cultural, medical, and recreational programs and facilities. Manhattan rates among the best classic college towns in the country, ranking #2 in the last two years in Livability\u2019s list of the 10 Best College Towns, and Forbes magazine ranked Manhattan #3 in the nation for best small places for businesses and careers. Worksite Description This position is on-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or Ed.D. in communication sciences and disorders or closely related field (ABD considered with an anticipated completion date within one year of hire) Earned Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) Eligibility for Kansas licensure as a speech-language pathologist Demonstrated or emerging record of scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications and/or external funding commensurate with career stage Evidence of, or clear potential for, excellence in teaching at the graduate and/or undergraduate level Effective interpersonal and communication skills suitable for graduate student mentorship, didactic teaching, and interprofessional collaboration To be considered for the rank of associate professor: Established, sustained research program with documented record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with rank Evidence of securing or competing for extramural funding from relevant agencies The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Specialization in dysphagia, adult neurogenic communication disorders, motor speech, and/or neuroanatomy Clinical supervision experience with graduate student clinicians in university or medical settings Engagement with a variety of clinical populations and culturally responsive, person-centered care Record of, or clear interest in, collaborative and/or interdisciplinary research Experience with, or interest in, pursuing external funding from federal agencies (i.e., NIH, NSF, HRSA, IES) Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Statement of research interests and plans (2 pages maximum) Contact information for three professional references Inquiries about the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Bob Garcia, at rgarcia@ksu.edu with the subject line: CSD Faculty Search. Application Window Applications close on: October 20, 2026 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ececf745 Last Name (required) db4d88f3 Email (required) 95f4e8ac Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4bff65cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education / Instructional Health Profession Education / Instructional Health Profession Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) ca4cf85a Last Name (required) fef4e6ff Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later a4181216 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) eb084e8b Last Name (required) 8a5367ca Email (required) 957c4fc3 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job ed3d7a35 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 86b9d399 Last Name (required) f28e84d6 Email (required) a4c2cf23 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 00322bb5 Last Name (required) 3766954e Email (required) 9305272c Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fellow-post-doc-manhattan-kansas-united-states-f6b545b7-5258-4eb0-8799-07aa4f87ef5e": {"title": "Fellow (Post Doc)", "description": "Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fellow (Post Doc) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fellow (Post Doc) Apply Now Fellow (Post Doc) Post-Doctoral position for independent research including but not limited to viruses such as Influenza, African swine fever, Vesicular Stomatitus, Rift Valley Fever, Monkey Pox and other select agents under both BSL-2 and BSL-3 bio-containment conditions. Duties would include planning and conducting experiments; writing and editing manuscripts/articles; establishing procedures and techniques; and provide educational guidance to students. This position is part of a very busy, successful research team whose main goal is to develop rationally designed vaccines and diagnostics against high-consequence foreign animal, emerging and zoonotic disease threats. The position requires the individual to display critical thinking and independent judgement as it relates to ongoing and new molecular, viral research with direct guidance from the Research Science Manager and Primary Investigator. The research is conducted at the BSL2 and BSL3 level of containment and utilizes several select target animal models such as pigs, cows, chickens and mice. The position requires the acquisition and maintenance of a DOJ Select Agent clearance. 520391 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Diagnostic Medicne Pathobiolog Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Oct 26 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Post-Doctoral position for independent research including but not limited to viruses such as Influenza, African swine fever, Vesicular Stomatitus, Rift Valley Fever, Monkey Pox and other select agents under both BSL-2 and BSL-3 bio-containment conditions. Duties would include planning and conducting experiments; writing and editing manuscripts/articles; establishing procedures and techniques; and provide educational guidance to students. This position is part of a very busy, successful research team whose main goal is to develop rationally designed vaccines and diagnostics against high-consequence foreign animal, emerging and zoonotic disease threats. The position requires the individual to display critical thinking and independent judgement as it relates to ongoing and new molecular, viral research with direct guidance from the Research Science Manager and Primary Investigator. The research is conducted at the BSL2 and BSL3 level of containment and utilizes several select target animal models such as pigs, cows, chickens and mice. The position requires the acquisition and maintenance of a DOJ Select Agent clearance. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Minimum of DVM with graduate degree \u2013 MS or PhD in science related field The degree requirement is necessary to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: DVM with Masters or PhD in immunology, molecular biology, virology, or related field >5 yrs. Molecular laboratory experience \u2013 PCR, RT-PCR, cloning, cell culture techniques, western blotting, affinity purification of recombinant proteins using eukaryotic/prokaryotic cells or cell-free systems, conducting safety and immunogenicity studies, immunological assays, virological assays, poster presentations and/or presentation at local, university or national meetings. Ability to work with animals in the BSL2 and BSL3 level of biocontainment. Experience working or conducting studies with animals \u2013 rodents, food animals, and/or companion animals. Molecular or virological laboratory experience - virus isolation, virus purification, virus titration, western blotting, affinity purification of recombinant proteins using eukaryotic/prokaryotic cells or cell-free systems, conducting safety. Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Information for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: October 26, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $39,227 - $66,667 annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 92444e74 Last Name (required) 8e167b8a Email (required) 8e2e66c5 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 66692091 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 4658bfb3 Last Name (required) bda88b33 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later d6089342 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 99654551 Last Name (required) af782f7a Email (required) 6411ea5b Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job c84f9798 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Man