advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 6ef71847 Last Name (required) 37aacc8d Email (required) 3bb24620 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) c2e169b9 Last Name (required) 9b3c750b Email (required) 44ded086 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/associate-director-of-research-and-evaluation-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Associate Director of Research and Evaluation", "description": "Associate Director of Research and Evaluation - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Associate Director of Research and Evaluation - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director of Research and Evaluation Apply Now Associate Director of Research and Evaluation Reporting to the Executive Director of Applied Learning, the Associate Director of Research and Evaluation serves as the university's lead researcher and evaluator for the Applied Learning Experience (ALE) initiative. 522322 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Staley School of Leadership Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 8 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site About This Role Reporting to the Executive Director of Applied Learning, the Associate Director of Research and Evaluation serves as the university's lead researcher and evaluator for the Applied Learning Experience (ALE) initiative. This position provides leadership for the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of a comprehensive university-wide assessment and evaluation framework that measures the impact of applied learning on student success, engagement, and institutional priorities. The Associate Director operates with a high degree of autonomy and professional discretion, independently establishing research priorities, evaluation methodologies, data collection strategies, and reporting processes. As the university's primary subject matter expert on applied learning assessment, this position synthesizes complex institutional, qualitative, and quantitative data to inform strategic decision making by university leadership and guide the future direction of the ALE initiative. The Associate Director collaborates extensively with academic colleges, faculty, institutional research personnel, student affairs professionals, and university administrators to ensure stakeholders engage in data-informed planning and continuous improvement efforts. Through research, scholarship, and evaluation leadership, this position advances institutional goals while contributing to national conversations regarding experiential and applied learning practices in higher education. In addition, the Associate Director provides day-to-day leadership and oversight of graduate research assistants and other research personnel supporting evaluation and assessment initiatives. Core Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Institutional Impact - 30% Lead the development and execution of the university-wide research, assessment, and evaluation strategy for the Applied Learning Experience initiative Independently identify emerging assessment needs, establish evaluation priorities, and recommend strategic improvements that strengthen institutional effectiveness and student outcomes Advise the Executive Director matters related to applied learning assessment, program effectiveness, and evidence-based decision making Develop recommendations for policy, practice, and resource allocation based on research findings and evaluation outcomes Represent the university in institutional, regional, and national conversations related to applied learning, assessment, and experiential education Research, Assessment, and Evaluation Leadership - 30% Design, implement, and continuously refine comprehensive qualitative and quantitative assessment frameworks measuring the effectiveness and impact of applied learning initiatives Lead the creation of research questions, study designs, assessment instruments, and evaluation methodologies aligned with university strategic priorities Independently conduct sophisticated qualitative research initiatives, including focus groups, interviews, and thematic analysis involving faculty, students, alumni, and community partners Partner with Office of Data, Assessment and Institutional Research, data systems personnel, and analysts to establish effective data collection processes and ensure the integrity of university-wide ALE metrics Integrate and synthesize information from multiple data sources to identify trends, assess outcomes, and inform strategic planning efforts Produce comprehensive annual and multi-year evaluation reports used by university leadership, accrediting agencies, external stakeholders, and funding partners Data Strategy and Decision Support - 15% Translate complex data into actionable recommendations that support institutional planning, continuous improvement, and strategic decision making Develop executive-level reports, dashboards, presentations, and summaries that communicate research findings to a variety of audiences Evaluate the effectiveness of current initiatives and recommend evidence-based enhancements to maximize program impact Serve as the primary authority for interpretation and application of ALE assessment data across the institution Research Leadership and Scholarly Contributions - 15% Lead the execution of the institutional ALE research agenda and ensure all research activities align with university goals and best practices in the field Maintain a visible national scholarly presence through peer-reviewed publications, books, conference presentations, and invited speaking engagements Identify emerging trends and best practices in experiential education and recommend innovative approaches for institutional adoption Establish collaborative research partnerships with internal and external stakeholders to advance knowledge within the field Personnel Leadership and Stakeholder Engagement - 10% Provide direct supervision, mentoring, performance management, and day-to-day oversight of graduate research assistants and student employees supporting research and evaluation activities Coordinate research activities across multiple academic and administrative units while fostering strong collaborative relationships with stakeholders throughout the university Serve as the primary liaison and recruiter for faculty and student participants, ensuring effective communication regarding research activities, assessment results, and continuous improvement efforts Provide support for adjacent faculty research projects to include data dashboards Facilitate a culture of evidence-based decision making through presentations, workshops, and consultations with campus partners About Us The Mary Lynn and Warren Staley School of Leadership at Kansas State University is a values-centered learning community that provides academic, co-curricular, and applied learning experiences to students across the university with the purpose of developing bold, curious, and connected learners to address our world\u2019s most complex challenges. A focus on incubating new initiatives, and building and strengthening partnerships has allowed the Staley School to evolve in new and diverse ways \u2013 launching new academic programs and becoming home to additional university-wide programs and initiatives, committed to enriching learning both in and out of the classroom. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and nine years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Education, Educational Leadership, Higher Education, Assessment, Research Methods, or a closely related field Ten years of professional experience in experiential education, applied learning, educational assessment, institutional research, program evaluation, or a related field Five years of progressively responsible leadership experience, including strategic planning, project leadership, personnel supervision, or administrative oversight Demonstrated experience designing and leading complex qualitative and quantitative research initiatives Proven ability to synthesize large and complex data sets into actionable recommendations for organizational or institutional leaders Distinguished record of scholarly achievement evidenced through peer-reviewed publications, books, grants, presentations, or other recognized contributions to the field Experience leading university-wide assessment, accreditation, evaluation, or institutional effectiveness initiatives Experience supervising graduate assistants, professional staff, or research personnel Demonstrated success influencing organizational strategy through data-informed recommendations and assessment findings Expertise communicating complex research findings to executive leaders, faculty, and external stakeholders Active involvement in national organizations focused on experiential education, assessment, institutional research, or student success Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume List of 3 or more professional references Application Window Applications close on: November 8th, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 79,926.00 - $ 110,000.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f778d415 Last Name (required) a8d09521 Email (required) 9ed921d1 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 303675f5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Education / Instructional Research / Scientific / Grants Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Education / Instructional Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 