independent experimental design and execution, strong technical expertise, and the ability to coordinate team-based research activities. 521382 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Anatomy & Physiology Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Research Associate to contribute to multiple vaccine development and evaluation projects. Working with minimal supervision from the Principal Investigator, this position requires independent experimental design and execution, strong technical expertise, and the ability to coordinate team-based research activities. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a master's degree and two years of relevant experience. (Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager.) The degree requirement ensures candidates possess advanced research skills, data analysis expertise and scientific writing ability in order to independently execute complex research tasks, interpret findings and contribute to scholarly publications. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and intensive experiential learning inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree (or higher) in microbiology, immunology, virology, animal science, biology, or a related field Or BS degree with demonstrated hands-on experience in cell culture, molecular biology, and immunoassays Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume 3. Contact information of three professional references Application Window Applications close: November 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $50,000 - $70,000 annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 7e458b26 Last Name (required) 00d4ae00 Email (required) 612ac74a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: c8196156 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 8c0a2533 Last Name (required) e2e07d24 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later a1b386ae Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) fe77e967 Last Name (required) ce65c465 Email (required) 23b7d5a6 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job d08eb911 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Associate Director of Research and Evaluation Manhattan Staley School of Leadership Assistant Scientist Manhattan Agronomy Assistant Chef Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to liv