cal pathologists to provide locum support. The locum will be responsible for the review of cytology samples, secondary review of select hematology cases, and consultation on clinical chemistry, urinalysis, and serum protein electrophoresis, as needed. The locum will provide daily support to interns on cases. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Complete the application and submit a CV. Application Window Applications close on: October 31, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range 10,000 bi-weekly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) fbd0f3fa Last Name (required) 4a404597 Email (required) 4cc1df57 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: a016c3fb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Temporary Part-time Temporary Part-time Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) edb06709 Last Name (required) d3805379 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 99cd7aa2 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 6b5d222b Last Name (req