w Assistant Chef Join our culinary team and lead catering production for a thriving dining program! Supervise staff, drive quality and efficiency, and create exceptional event experiences. If you're passionate about food and leadership, we want to hear from you! 522375 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Assistant Chef oversees daily food production for the Housing and Dining Services catering program, ensuring the safe, efficient, and high-quality preparation of catering orders and event meals. This position supervises culinary staff, coordinates production workflows, and maintains established food safety and quality standards to deliver exceptional catering services. Key responsibilities of this position include: production operations management staff supervision and leadership catering production coordination food safety, sanitation, and regulatory compliance inventory and resource management About Us Housing and Dining Services (HDS) is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. We share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. HDS provides affordable, safe and engaging accommodations for more than 5,000 residents and find unique ways to support their academic pursuits. Additionally, we offer a variety of event spaces, dining and catering options for both on and off-campus events. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. What a great team to be part of! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires two years of relevant experience with one year of experience at the supervisory level. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license upon employment. Preferred Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Three years of experience in commercial, large scale food service operations including food preparation and kitchen production. Experience working in university, catering, banquet, or conference dining environments. Experience coordinating the work of culinary staff in a food service environment. Knowledge of food safety, sanitation practices, and kitchen safety procedures. Experience supervising staff in a high-volume food service environment. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Effective written and oral communication skills. Additional Role Information: ServSafe Food Protection Manager certification or ability to obtain within six months of hire. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Letter of Interest Names and contact information for three professional references Online application Application Window Applications close on: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.04 - $25.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) bf45a001 Last Name (required) cbd923f7 Email (required) b3520565 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f9403d20 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Food Safety / Science / Systems Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States M