ob opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/cook-jp-s-sports-grill-manhattan-kansas-united-states-d4248b7b-d3f9-4ce8-8f0f-5a59c5c07f17": {"title": "Cook (JP's Sports Grill)", "description": "Cook (JP's Sports Grill) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Cook (JP's Sports Grill) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Cook (JP's Sports Grill) Apply Now Cook (JP's Sports Grill) Participate in daily food production and service in a fast-paced restaurant environment. Train and direct student staff, ensure food quality and safety, manage schedules and supplies, and maintain high standards for sanitation, service, and teamwork. 522365 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 21 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site About This Role Participates in food production for JP's Sports Grill , an on-campus retail restaurant serving the local community in addition to campus based faculty, staff and students. The position has direct impact on the dining satisfaction level of customers. The position offers a 40 hour per week schedule, a great work-life balance and a generous benefit package. Key responsibilities include: \u2022 Culinary Operations: Prepare and serve high-quality food using made-to-order cooking methods and standardized recipes in a fast-paced restaurant environment. \u2022 Coordinate Daily Production: Plan food production, monitor supplies and quantities, track yields, and ensure meals are ready on time for excellent customer service. \u2022 Lead & Train Student Staff: Assign, train, coach, and support student employees in food preparation, service, safety, sanitation, and efficient work practices. \u2022 Ensure Food Quality & Safety: Maintain high standards for food quality, portioning, presentation, temperature, sanitation, and HACCP food safety practices. \u2022 Support Staffing & Operations: Adjust schedules, coordinate daily assignments, and step into culinary duties as needed to keep operations running smoothly. \u2022 Maintain a Safe, Clean Kitchen: Oversee cleaning and equipment maintenance while promoting safe, sanitary, and efficient work areas. \u2022 Build a Positive Team Environment: Foster strong relationships with students, coworkers, and management while promoting professionalism, teamwork, and respect. \u2022 Manage Resources & Improve Operations: Help maximize the effective use of food, supplies, labor, and equipment while identifying opportunities for operational improvements. \u2022 Stay Organized & Accountable: Complete production records, participate in training and meetings, communicate operational needs, and consistently uphold established standards. About Us Housing and Dining Services (HDS) is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. We share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. HDS provides affordable, safe and engaging accommodations for more than 5,000 residents and find unique ways to support their academic pursuits. Additionally, we offer a variety of event spaces, dining and catering options for both on and off-campus events. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. What a great team to be part of! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: High school graduation/GED 1-3 years cooking experience in a restaurant setting Considerable knowledge of \u201cfrom scratch\u201d batch food preparation, equipment, health sanitation, and safety procedures The ability to develop and maintain congenial work relationships with other staff and customers Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions Ability to learn to perform basic math computations; to accurately weigh and measure ingredients Ability to present prepared food attractively Ability to use and care for equipment and handle food safely while preparing high quality products Prefer ServSafe certification Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: on-line application Application Window Applications close on: October 21, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.00 - $18.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) e8db514b Last Name (required) 96927308 Email (required) 35f15b3e Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: c3e74180 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Food Safety / Science / Systems Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 11a52b70 Last Name (required) d0579c8f Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 1e9a3ad7 Save Now! Please 