alifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 0c2fa8e3 Last Name (required) 31897def Email (required) 4aa5d1c2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) ace88761 Last Name (required) 967ecccf Email (required) 1c7e8259 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/electrician-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Electrician", "description": "Electrician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Electrician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Electrician Apply Now Electrician This position exists to provide highly skilled electrician support to the university through construction, maintenance and repair duties to provide a safe environment for students, faculty, staff and guests. 522313 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 29 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to provide highly skilled electrician support to the university through construction, maintenance and repair duties to provide a safe environment for students, faculty, staff and guests. About Us The Division of Facilities' maintenance personnel conduct routine maintenance on building systems and equipment to ensure the operational reliability of our campus' building systems. This maintenance involves regular, scheduled service to maintain equipment functionality without the need for immediate repairs. Many of the older buildings have systems and equipment that have exceeded their expected lifespan, highlighting the value of a strong preventive maintenance program Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer at least four years of experience in commercial electrical work, with two years at the journey level. Knowledge of high voltage and commercial electrical practices would be helpful. Additional Role Information: Become certified as a Class 1 Asbestos worker during the probationary period and maintain it. Work involves considerable physical exertion to transport equipment and supplies associated with the position weighing 50 pounds or more unassisted on a repetitive basis daily. Ability required to climb and work from ladders; work from bucket trucks and man lifts; work in confined areas and in strenuous body positions on a repetitive basis daily. DAILY: State vehicles, hand drills, test equipment, hand conduit bender, two-say radio, computer. WEEKLY: Bucket truck, percussion stud gun and hydraulic conduit bender. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Complete Application Application Window Applications close on: 10-29-2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $20.30 - $31.45 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c16c242f Last Name (required) 9e05d35d Email (required) ae0cfd38 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 3733a8e7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 975e237b Last Name (required) 281f29dc Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later cec97eac Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 0e7891e8 Last Name (required) 99c87eb7 Email (required) 08015c32 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send t