 team member! This position will provide a clean and safe environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors at the Peters Recreation Complex. 522058 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Recreational Services Peters Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site About This Role This position exists to provide a clean and safe environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors at the Peters Recreation Complex. About Us Recreational Services\u2019 mission is to develop, promote and manage the administration of recreational and fitness facilities, services and programs for the campus community at Kansas State University. Active and healthy lifestyles enhance opportunities for continuance of personal and professional maintenance and growth. These lifestyles are positively affected by the quality and quantity of the services, programs and facilities we provide. Recreational Services promotes student development and provides leadership opportunities in a diverse setting for its participants and employees. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: None Required Preferred Qualifications: Preferred Education: High School Diploma Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in an institutional setting; Experience using commercial cleaning equipment; Stable work history; Knowledge in custodial procedures; Ability to work around a large participant and employee base; Ability to work with pressure of a schedule that requires adapting to a varying routine Additional Role Information: Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment Ability to operate and control walk-behind and riding scrubbers Ability to work around cleaning and floor chemicals Ability to transport heavy objects (up to 50lbs) Work is generally performed by standing and walking during the shift Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Please submit the online application form Application Window Applications close on October 28th, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 48892040 Last Name (required) 75670370 Email (required) 674dc374 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 7cf4ce14 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) a3fdc0b9 Last Name (required) b649bd70 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0045a4d4 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) f4902bb4 Last Name (required) e0652711 Email (required) e5b55cd3 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 68597d39 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Associate Director of Research and Evaluation Manhattan Staley School of Leadership Assistant Scientist Manhattan Agronomy Assistant Chef Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. 