 fcf478a9 Last Name (required) 4e2b92f5 Email (required) bcd99c6f Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-of-industry-and-strategic-partnerships-olathe-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships", "description": "Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships - Olathe, Kansas, United States Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships - Olathe, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships Apply Now Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships K-State Olathe (https://olathe.k-state.edu/) seeks a Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships to lead K-State Olathe\u2019s efforts to develop and expand strategic relationships with corporations, industry partners, community organizations, and regional stakeholders. 522386 Olathe, Kansas, United States K-State Olathe Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 1 2026 - 23:55 CST Hybrid eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Director of Industry and Strategic Partnerships leads K-State Olathe\u2019s ( https://olathe.k-state.edu/) efforts to develop and expand strategic relationships with corporations, industry partners, employers, community organizations, and regional stakeholders. The position is responsible for identifying, developing, and converting external partnership opportunities into measurable outcomes that advance enrollment growth, workforce development, applied research, fee-for-service activities, and diversified revenue generation for K-State Olathe. Working closely with the K-State Office of External Engagement and other university partners, the director identifies organizational and community needs, connects partners with university expertise and resources, and collaborates across campus to develop customized education, workforce, research, and engagement solutions. The position also strengthens K-State Olathe\u2019s role as a trusted civic and regional partner by supporting initiatives that expand learner access, address workforce and community needs, and create measurable regional impact. The director represents the Dean and CEO in selected corporate, civic, community, and university settings and supports the implementation of K-State Olathe\u2019s strategic priorities through relationship management, partnership development, data-informed planning, and cross-campus collaboration. Success in this position is measured by the development and conversion of partnership opportunities into tangible outcomes, including enrollment growth, workforce-training revenue, fee-for-service activity, industry -sponsored research, and other strategic partnerships that advance K-State Olathe\u2019s mission and financial sustainability. Specific Job Responsibilities A. Industry Partnerships & Business Development - 60% Serve as the industry partnership and business development lead for K-State Olathe, developing partnerships that advance enrollment growth, workforce development, applied research, fee-for-service agreements, professional and continuing education, and other revenue-generating initiatives. Develop and execute an industry engagement and business development strategy aligned with K-State Olathe\u2019s strategic priorities, academic strengths, research capabilities, and regional workforce needs. Be accountable for achieving annual partnership-development, revenue-generation, enrollment, and engagement goals established jointly with the dean and CEO. Develop and manage a portfolio of partnership opportunities with defined annual targets for new agreements, employer-sponsored enrollment, workforce training contracts, applied research activity, and revenue generation. In collaboration with the K-State Office of External Engagement and other university partners, lead consultative partnership-development activities, including prospect identification, outreach, relationship cultivation, organizational needs assessment, solution design, proposal development, agreement negotiation, implementation, and evaluation. Develop employer partnerships that result in measurable enrollment growth, contract training revenue, customized workforce solutions, and employer-sponsored educational pathways. Partner with Professional and Continuing Education leadership, academic departments, faculty, and program managers to translate employer needs into customized training, professional development, certificates, microcredentials, and workforce education solutions. Maintain and actively manage a comprehensive CRM-based partnership pipeline, including prospect qualification, opportunity tracking, revenue forecasting, and outcome reporting. Identify, qualify, develop, and convert partnership opportunities into executed agreements and measurable institutional outcomes. B. Civic, Community & Regional Engagement - 25% Develop and maintain strategic relationships with civic, workforce, economic development, and community organizations that support K-State Olathe\u2019s enrollment, partnership, workforce, research, and revenue objectives. Cultivate relationships with chambers of commerce, economic-development organizations, workforce agencies, community foundations, educational institutions, and professional associations to identify partnerships and growth opportunities. Represent K-State Olathe in regional civic organizations, community initiatives, industry councils, workforce-development groups, and economic-development convenings that align with campus priorities. Identify and facilitate opportunities for K-State Olathe faculty, staff, students, and programs to contribute to regional initiatives while advancing institutional priorities and community impact. C. Strategic Partnerships & Executive Representation - 10% Represent the Dean and CEO at corporate, community, and university engagements as assigned. Serve as a liaison between K-State Olathe and K-State units in Manhattan and Salina to coordinate corporate and community partnership strategies, share institutional capabilities, and reduce duplication of outreach. Lead the development and coordination of partnership agreements, business plans, MOUs, and related documents in collaboration with legal counsel, risk management, finance, and other appropriate university offices. Prepare executive briefings, partner profiles, engagement strategies, presentations, talking points, and follow-up plans for high-priority corporate and community relationships. Supervise unit personnel as the strategic engagement function grows. D. Special Projects & Strategic Initiatives - 5% Advance the K-State Olathe Strategic Plan by tracking, evaluating, and reporting progress toward corporate engagement, civic engagement, enrollment, workforce development, and partnership goals. Support pilot programs, regional initiatives, and emerging partnership opportunities identified by the Dean and CEO. Undertake additional strategic assignments that advance K-State Olathe\u2019s regional visibility, learner access, financial sustainability, and community impact. About Us Kansas State University Olathe, founded in 2011, is the newest campus in the K-State system and serves Johnson County and the Greater Kansas City region. As a partner in the Johnson County Education and Research Triangle, the campus supports higher education through a unique local investment. K-State Olathe focuses on industry-ready education, professional development, applied research, and regional workforce needs, with programs and partnerships in areas such as food science, animal health, advanced manufacturing, supply chain, community health, and food as medicine. Through academic programs, professional workshops, research facilities, and event space, the campus connects students, professionals, businesses, and community partners to education and innovation that create real-world impact. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid eligible . This position is hybrid eligible; however, we require the first 90 days to be 100% on-site to allow for training and onboarding. After that period, hybrid eligibility will be discussed with the supervisor. It is important to note that when duties require in-person attendance, this position requires a commitment to being in the office. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) \u2022 Ten years of relevant experience \u2022 Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience \u2022 Valid Driver's License Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher \u2022 Excellent writing and executive communication skills with a focus on business communications and presentations as evidenced by application materials. \u2022 Demonstrated success developing partnerships that resulted in measurable organizational growth, revenue generation, enrollments, contracts, sponsored programs, or other quantifiable outcomes. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to develop opportunities from prospect identification through implementation, resulting in measurable business, educational, workforce, research, or revenue outcomes. \u2022 Experience managing a business-development, employer-engagement, or partnership pipeline. \u2022 Experience developing proposals, scopes of work, partnership agreements, or service contracts. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to translate organizational capabilities into externally funded opportunities. \u2022 Experience working with industry associations, chambers of commerce, workforce-development organizations, or economic-development entities \u2022 Experience working in a complex organization with multiple stakeholders across both internal and external clients \u2022 CRM proficiency for tracking pipeline and partner engagement \u2022 Attention to detail \u2022 Proven ability to execute multiple projects and meet tight deadlines Additional Role Information: \u2022 Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. \u2022 This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, with a minimum of three on-site days per week after 90 days. \u2022 Must be able to work some nights and weekends as needed to support events, conferences, and industry or community engagements. \u2022 Travel between K-State campuses in Olathe, Manhattan and Salina as well as within the greater Kansas City region as needed. Occasional state and national travel. A valid motor vehicle operator\u2019s license with an acceptable driving record required as well as the ability to travel by air. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: \u2022 Cover Letter or Letter of Interest indicating your qualifications and interest in the position \u2022 Resume \u2022 Three (3) Professional References with contact information Incomplete applications will not be considered. Application Window Applications close on: November 1, 2026. Application review will begin on or after the close date. Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $85,000 - $95,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8725e695 Last Name (required) 04887272 Email (required) b0342e4a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: ba321f9f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Community Development / Community Vitality Executive / Director / Management Administrative / Professional Business / Accounting / Finance Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Community Development / Community Vitality Executive / Director / Management Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Olathe, Kansas, United States Olathe, Kansas, United States Worksite Hybrid eligible Hybrid eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) a606e778 Last Name (required) 5ead39b4 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 15c7050f Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) e66ab447 Last Name (required) 53e5b91f Email (required) 845767cc Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7d171765 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Associate Director of Research and Evaluation Manhattan Staley School of Leadership Assistant Scientist Manhattan Agronomy Assistant Chef Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside the state of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) f7e5b66e Last Name (required) 67f59122 Email (required) d71c279c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 9950bc03 Last Name (required) 451f116e Email (required) 5d4980ed Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/animal-technician-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-9c92e85f-4956-4641-9070-a1f9dd2e380e": {"title": "Animal Technician II", "description": "Animal Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Animal Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Animal Technician II Apply Now Animal Technician II The DTRC Animal Technician II is responsible for daily care of the cattle housed at the DTRC. The incumbent will be responsible for routine care of the cattle at the DTRC, ranging from newborn calves to lactating cows. This position will require operation of machinery relevant to animal care, including skid loaders. 522387 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Animal Sciences & Industry Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The DTRC Animal Technician II is responsible for daily care of the cattle housed at the DTRC. The incumbent will be responsible for routine care of the cattle at the DTRC, ranging from newborn calves to lactating cows. This position will require operation of machinery relevant to animal care, including skid loaders. About Us The Department of Animal Sciences and Industry (ASI) serves students, livestock producers and the animal and food industries through teaching, research and education. The Dept. of ASI prepares students for careers in the animal and food industries. The curriculum includes the study of nutrition, reproduction, genetics, behavior, meat science and food science with production, management, and agribusiness skills. Students are given sound professional and scientific skills, a broad education and experience for contributing to our communities across the nation and abroad. Students receive excellent advisement and mentorship from faculty and professional staff and participate in extracurricular activities to develop skills to become industry leaders. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience. Some positions may require additional education (or relevant experience) that will be specified in the position description. Various training and/or certification may be required Preferred Qualifications: One year of work with livestock Ability to work independently Availability to work some weekends and/or holidays 2-3 years of dairy cattle and milking experience Experience operating large machinery Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: KSU Page Up online application Letter of Interest Resume List of three references with email addresses and phone numbers listed Application Window Applications close on:10/28/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.36-$24.53 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 4550c6c8 Last Name (required) ec44066f Email (required) ca389fbb Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: a6c82232 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Animal Sciences / Livestock Agriculture Animal Sciences / Livestock Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 755a7896 Last Name (required) 8531284d Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 7de06fa1