ist - Other, Kansas, United States Marketing & Member Strategist - Other, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Marketing & Member Strategist Apply Now Marketing & Member Strategist The Journalism Education Association is seeking a creative, strategic and data-driven marketing & member strategist to strengthen our brand, elevate our communications, and drive membership growth and engagement. 522414 Other, Kansas AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST Remote eligible About This Role The Journalism Education Association is seeking a creative, strategic and data-driven marketing & member strategist to strengthen our brand, elevate our communications, and drive membership growth and engagement. This dynamic role leads integrated marketing and communications across digital, social media, email, web and print channels while developing strategies to recruit, retain, and connect members with the resources and benefits they value. The ideal candidate is a strong storyteller, skilled communicator, and collaborative problem-solver who combines marketing expertise, digital proficiency, and a passion for member service to advance JEA\u2019s mission of supporting journalism educators and scholastic journalism. About Us Journalism Education Association (JEA) is a member association that supports free and responsible scholastic journalism by providing resources and educational opportunities, by promoting professionalism, by encouraging and rewarding student excellence and teacher achievement, and by fostering an atmosphere which encompasses unity. JEA is officially headquartered at Kansas State University (K-State) and is considered a sponsored program of K-State. Therefore, K-State administers the JEA benefits entailing a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, life insurance, generous retirement plan contributions, paid time off- vacation, sick, and holidays. To see what benefits are available, please visit: https://www.k-state.edu/hcs/benefits Worksite Description This position is . Remote work is granted at the discretion of the direct supervisor. An employee who is working remotely must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, regulations filings, or tax requirements. Review K-State\u2019s remote work policy details for more information. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and seven years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 4+ years experience in marketing/communication, membership recruitment/retention, in similar organizations or related functions. \u2022 Understanding of or familiarity of volunteer-driven organizations, nonprofit/associations. \u2022 Proven success leading enterprise-wide integrated marketing and communication and able to devise strategies and implement plans across multimedia platforms. \u2022 Experience managing brand identity and organizational messaging. \u2022 Proficient in Adobe Creative Suite and being able to design for print, social media, web, etc. efficiently. \u2022 Proficient in member database management. \u2022 Proficient in member and marketing tools and data analytics including the Google environment and Google Analytics. \u2022 Experience in AP Style. \u2022 Proficient in up-to-date social media algorithms and utilizing current platforms. \u2022 Strong skills in marketing automation, AMS, CRM, CMS and being able to manage content on a website, understand the backend and plugins. \u2022 Strong computer skills and communication collaboration tools (e.g. for project management). \u2022 Maintain confidentiality and utmost professionalism. \u2022 Excellent organizational and time management skills and the ability to meet deadlines. \u2022 Strong interpersonal skills and commitment to a high level of customer service. \u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills to interact effectively with a variety of stakeholders, staff, boards, perspectives and various funding entities. \u2022 Strong writing, content development and storytelling skills. \u2022 Highly strategic, analytical thinker with the ability to translate programs into compelling narratives. \u2022 Ability and willingness to travel and represent JEA several times per year (including at the spring/April and fall/November conventions). Additional Role Information: \u2022 Willingness and ability to travel several times annually and occasionally work evenings or weekends in support of association activities. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Resume Application Window Applications close on: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $55,000- $65,000 annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 6ffe681b Last Name (required) 47d9c103 Email (required) e3d49dbe Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 9f3d6f34 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Other, Kansas, United States Other, Kansas, United States Worksite Remote eligible Remote eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Content missing Share this job with a 