 512836c5 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/landscape-technician-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-04a94465-9746-4fc1-81b1-b3fd6bfa7131": {"title": "Landscape Technician II", "description": "Landscape Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Landscape Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Landscape Technician II Apply Now Landscape Technician II Housing and Dining Services seeks a Landscape Technician II maintain healthy, attractive campus landscapes. The role includes pest identification and treatment, turf and plant care, and supporting landscape installations and seasonal grounds work. 522422 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Our Housing and Dining Services Facilities Management grounds team create and maintain a safe, aesthetically pleasing outdoor environment enjoyed by the K-State community\u2014and we\u2019re looking for a Landscape Technician II to be part of this team. In this hands-on role, you\u2019ll help protect and enhance campus landscapes through expert care of turf and plant materials. From identifying and treating pests to supporting landscape installations and seasonal campus operations, your work will directly contribute to maintaining the welcoming environment that students, faculty, staff, and visitors experience every day. What You\u2019ll Do: \u2022 Diagnose and treat diseases, weeds, and insect issues affecting turf grass and landscape materials \u2022 Apply best management practices for landscape and turf care \u2022 Identify, monitor, assess, and control pest populations using appropriate products \u2022 Evaluate and select treatments for weeds and insects \u2022 Assist with landscape and hardscape installation projects \u2022 Perform general grounds maintenance \u2022 Transport furniture, equipment, and materials as needed \u2022 Help keep campus safe during winter by removing snow and ice and treating outdoor surfaces before, during, and after inclement weather About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, self-operated auxiliary department serving more than 5,000 students that call the K-State campus home. This \"home away from home\" meets more than the basic needs of students living with us \u2014 we provide affordable, safe and engaging accommodations and services for our residents, while finding unique ways to support them in their academic pursuits. We pride ourselves on taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. YOU can help make our residents and guests feel welcome and comfortable! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires six months of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Prefer high school graduation/GED Familiarity with grounds/pest related chemicals and their application Familiarity with turf grasses and other landscape materials Experience working in an institutional grounds maintenance unit Familiarity with a variety of equipment and tools used in grounds maintenance Ability to read, interpret and work from sketches, blueprints and specifications Ability to complete concise and accurate reports and records Ability to plan and organize work Effective written and oral communication skills Ability to interact effectively with others Must obtain a Commercial Pesticide Applicators certificate in 3A and 3B within 6 months of appointment Additional Role Information: Weather related duties may require occasional evening, early morning or week-end hours. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Online application Application Window Applications close on: November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 - $19.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 115348e9 Last Name (required) 6104f522 Email (required) 241a0a8a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d59596bb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 3aa9e9fe Last Name (required) aafb6572 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0a8940a3 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name