his Role This position provides human resource activities for assigned reporting units served by the Provost Business Office team. Administrative services include compliance with university, State of Kansas and Federal policies, execution of the employee recruitment process, management of human resource payroll functions, time and leave, oversight of the performance management process, maintenance of employee records and providing benefits information all with a high level of excellent customer service. About Us The Office of the Provost provides administrative leadership for the university's academic enterprise, driving a culture of academic innovation and excellence in support of our Next-Gen K-State vision and goals. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and three years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Associate degree or bachelor's degree in human resources. Two or more years of relevant experience in human resources and/or payroll. Experience in data entry, payroll, recruitment, human resources, and customer service. Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent organizational skills Ability to determine priorities, exercise sound judgment and work independently Willingness to learn new software, to develop additional skills, and to engage in professional development Ability to exercise discretion and uphold confidentiality Demonstrated background or knowledge of human resource processes and policies Additional Role Information: Eligible to become a Notary Public upon employment Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on:November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.04-23.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) d394a2a3 Last Name (required) db269f53 Email (required) 4a3f4dc1 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 17892949 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) c7349e7e Last Name (required) 92d31eae Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 8a60eb0b Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) ff166111 Last Name (required) 65d62a8d Email (required) c3459049 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job ac970f37 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions capt