t follow-up to support high-quality patient care. This individual must maintain a professional, compassionate, and service-oriented attitude while learning the unique workflows and communication preferences of the clinical teams they support. Working hours for this position will be Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm. 522398 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 3 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Client Services Assistant to join our dedicated Small Animal Medicine team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This person will serve as the primary liaison between clients and the clinical care team within assigned Small Animal Medicine service areas. This role ensures smooth communication, accurate scheduling, and consistent follow-up to support high-quality patient care. This individual must maintain a professional, compassionate, and service-oriented attitude while learning the unique workflows and communication preferences of the clinical teams they support. Working hours for this position will be Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) One year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Prior customer service experience in a fast-paced environment. Two or more years of experience in a veterinary setting. Knowledge of medical terminology, diseases, and symptoms. Strong multi-tasking skills. Ability to make sound decisions in a stressful situation. Ability to prioritize and recognize the most effective & efficient process to accomplish the daily workflow. Excellent communication (written and verbal) and strong interpersonal skills. Adaptable to different computer systems/advanced computer skills. Flexibility and willingness to help other teammates. Ability to answer multiple phone lines. Ability to perform word processing and data entry procedures on a personal computer. Willing and able to master new techniques. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close: November 3, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.50 - $16.50 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f1a4f182 Last Name (required) 6be99842 Email (required) 9b98ca50 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 75082e9a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 6ab9d0b4 Last Name (required) 2068d2b4 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 26d7e84e Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 3884c082 Last Name (required) 9539d1e3 Email (required) 32dd90c6 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 0dafa9e4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 