 preferred - Doctorate in Veterinary Medicine or equivalent Additional Role Information: - Requirements include: interest in veterinary diagnostic medicine, excellent written and verbal communication skills, attention to detail, ability to arrive to perform after hours tests within 20 min. of being paged - Use of clinical pathology laboratory equipment (e.g., chemistry, blood gas, coagulation, and blood analyzers, centrifuges, and microscope). Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: December 1, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $44,634.98 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5e8f2c16 Last Name (required) c7bdb31e Email (required) d1500e53 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 3c585ab8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 23f77c5f Last Name (required) 538cf885 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later f9315e9f Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 05710f1a Last Name (required) 9cde56a6 Email (required) 73379935 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send