candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 9e6d45b8 Last Name (required) b7d11c47 Email (required) 5e9fe331 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) edcdd245 Last Name (required) 405e5096 Email (required) 585ac95e Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/office-specialist-iv-manhattan-kansas-united-states-1fb6afad-4322-4377-afc3-e3bdd75dea9f": {"title": "Office Specialist IV", "description": "Office Specialist IV - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Office Specialist IV - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Office Specialist IV Apply Now Office Specialist IV The Office of the President is inviting applications for an office specialist to serve as the welcoming first point of contact while managing daily office operations and providing administrative support, stakeholder communications, and project and event assistance for the President and Provost Offices. 522409 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Office of External Engagement Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 17 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position serves as the office manager and receptionist for the Office of the President and provides administrative support for both the Office of the President and Office of the Provost. The position greets visitors to the President\u2019s Office, prioritizes interactions for follow-up and ensures follow-through with stakeholder communications. The incumbent manages the office, ensures efficient day-to-day functioning and is relied upon to provide support for projects and events for the President and Provost Offices, as requested. This position reports to the deputy chief of staff. About Us The Office of the President serves as a central hub for leadership, strategy, and engagement at Kansas State University, supporting initiatives that advance the university's mission in teaching, research, service, and community impact. The office works across academic, student, research, government, and community-focused areas, bringing together leaders and partners to help shape the university's future and strengthen its impact throughout Kansas and beyond. Supported by a collaborative team of professionals, the office plays a vital role in fostering connections, advancing institutional priorities, and turning ambitious goals into meaningful outcomes. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires three years of relevant experience Preferred Qualifications: Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to interact courteously and professionally with all levels of university stakeholders Strong customer service orientation and commitment to the University\u2019s inclusive mission, with a proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Must be able to work in a fast-paced environment with demonstrated ability to handle multiple tasks, with a proven ability to work well under pressure. Excellent attention to detail and follow-through with the ability to support special projects Excellent verbal and written communication skills Expertise in Microsoft Office suite, particularly Outlook, Excel, Word, and PowerPoint Ability to exercise professionalism, discretion and integrity, especially pertaining to confidential matters Deep knowledge of the K-State organizational structure Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 17, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $19.00 \u2013 $24.00 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 94a0a4ce Last Name (required) 591ac386 Email (required) 00caf2c0 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: e70eebe1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Administrative / Professional Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (r