ell-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 7eb62c1a Last Name (required) 0e758440 Email (required) 02ef412b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) a8e4fe18 Last Name (required) 130f87c0 Email (required) 4d100c59 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/faculty-position-in-industrial-design-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Faculty Position in Industrial Design", "description": "Faculty Position in Industrial Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Faculty Position in Industrial Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Faculty Position in Industrial Design Apply Now Faculty Position in Industrial Design Join K-State\u2019s Industrial Design program as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice. Teach studios and courses in foundational design, furniture design, or visual communication. Starts Aug 2027. 522403 Manhattan 3670015040 Department of Design Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Jan 15 2027 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Industrial Design program at Kansas State University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month faculty position beginning August 2027. The successful candidate may be appointed as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice, depending on qualifications, academic preparation, and professional experience. We seek a collaborative and forward-looking designer and educator who will contribute to the continued growth of our Industrial Design program. The successful candidate will bring expertise in contemporary design practice, a commitment to student learning, and new perspectives that help prepare the next generation of industrial designers. The program seeks candidates with demonstrated expertise in foundational design, furniture design, and/or visual communication. Candidates should be able to connect design education with evolving professional practice. TEACHING RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will teach design studios and other courses across the Industrial Design curriculum, with assignments based on program needs and the candidate\u2019s expertise. Candidates should be prepared to: Teach undergraduate studios and courses primarily and, as appropriate to the appointment, graduate design courses. Develop and teach lectures, seminars, and other courses in two of the following areas: foundational design, furniture design, or visual communication. Integrate contemporary design methods, tools, technologies, and industry practices into teaching. Maintain current course content and contribute to curriculum development and continuous program improvement. Collaborate with faculty, students, alumni, industry partners, and the broader design community. Support industry and community collaborations, internships, and career development opportunities that connect students with professional practice. APPOINTMENT PATHWAYS Tenure Track Assistant Professor The tenure-track appointment supports an integrated commitment to teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and service. Teaching \u2014 65\u201370% Teach undergraduate and graduate design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate\u2019s expertise and program needs. Contribute to curriculum development, collaborative teaching, and the advancement of Industrial Design education. The teaching load is 14\u201316 credit hours per academic year, including 5-credit-hour studios and 2\u20133-credit-hour lectures or seminars. Research and Creative Scholarship \u2014 25\u201330% Develop and sustain a focused program of research and/or creative scholarship informed by the candidate\u2019s academic preparation, professional experience, teaching interests, or areas of design inquiry. Scholarly and creative work should advance Industrial Design and will form an important basis for promotion and tenure. Service \u2014 5\u201310% Contribute to the program, department, college, university, profession, and broader community through committee participation, curriculum initiatives, professional engagement, outreach, and related activities. Professor of Practice The Professor of Practice appointment emphasizes teaching excellence, professional expertise, and engagement with the Industrial Design profession. Teaching \u2014 80\u201390% Teach undergraduate Industrial Design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate\u2019s professional expertise and program needs, including courses related to professional practice. Bring substantial practice experience into the classroom and connect student learning with current industry methods, expectations, and opportunities. The typical teaching load is 14\u201318 credit hours per academic year, including 5-credit-hour studios and 2\u20134-credit-hour lectures or seminars. Service \u2014 10\u201320% Contribute to program, department, college, university, and community initiatives; student engagement; curriculum development; and professional communities. Strengthen relationships with alumni, industry partners, and employers, and identify opportunities for collaboration, internships, and student career development. About Us About Our Industrial Design Program The Industrial Design program is part of the Department of Design within Kansas State University\u2019s College of Architecture, Planning, and Design. The program offers multiple pathways to the Master of Industrial Design degree. Students entering from high school complete a five-year non-baccalaureate master\u2019s program, beginning with a foundation year in environmental studies and followed by four years of Industrial Design coursework, including a summer semester. Students with a previous bachelor\u2019s degree may complete an accelerated graduate pathway in two to three years. The curriculum combines design exploration, human-centered design, prototyping, visual communication, professional preparation, and an award-winning Furniture Design sequence. Internship and study-abroad embedded experiences expand students\u2019 academic and professional experience. Our goal is to prepare designers to address changing social, cultural, technological, and professional challenges through meaningful products, services, experiences, and systems. Faculty and students work in a collaborative interdisciplinary environment alongside Interior Architecture, Interior Design, Architecture, Landscape Architecture, and Regional and Community Planning. The department is housed in Seaton and Regnier Hall, with access to approximately 20,000 square feet of fabrication and research facilities supporting prototyping, experimentation, and hands-on learning. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: For Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher in Industrial Design, or a related field. Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate design studios across the curriculum. Ability to develop and teach lectures, seminars, or other courses related to the candidate\u2019s expertise and program needs. Demonstrated excellence in written and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. Demonstrated potential to develop and sustain research and/or creative scholarship related to the candidate\u2019s academic preparation, professional expertise, or areas of design inquiry. For Professor of Practice Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher in Industrial Design, Product Design, or related field. Six or more years of creative and/or professional practice experience in Industrial Design, Product Design, or a related field. Ability to teach undergraduate design studios across the curriculum. Ability to develop and teach courses related to professional practice in Industrial Design. Demonstrated excellence in written and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: For Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Preferred Qualifications Six or more years of creative and/or professional practice experience in Industrial Design, Product Design, or a related field. Previous experience teaching at the university level. Evidence of an emerging or established research and/or creative scholarship agenda. Experience contributing to curriculum development. Record of service or engagement within academic, professional, or design communities. Experience collaborating with industry, community partners, or interdisciplinary teams. For Professor of Practice Preferred Qualifications Ten or more years of professional practice in Industrial Design, Product Design, or related field. Previous teaching experience in higher education. A diverse professional design background spanning multiple industries or product categories. Experience leading or collaborating with interdisciplinary design and development teams. Evidence of professional leadership, mentorship, or significant contribution to the Industrial Design profession. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents in one PDF: Letter of interest addressing your qualifications and interest in the position. Resume or curriculum vitae. Portfolio of professional and/or creative work. Teaching portfolio, if applicable. Application Window Applications close on: January 15, 2027 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,000-$78,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5665fce8 Last Name (required) cd06c361 Email (required) 36b7ff86 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d77b52e2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education / Instructional Education / Instructional Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 0ed8711c Last Name (required) 8c19e237 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later dd4ea362 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 365d994d Last Name (required) 05ffc7f8 Email (required) cda757ab Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 4c9410ba Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 43a097da Last Name (required) 0d1fce76 Email (required) 044fb1e8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 739cd876 Last Name (required) 0a2f7861 Email (required) 4d4e4a6b Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/faculty-position-in-interior-design-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Faculty Position in Interior Design", "description": "Faculty Position in Interior Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Faculty Position in Interior Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Faculty Position in Interior Design Apply Now Faculty Position in Interior Design Teach courses across a CIDA-accredited interior design curriculum, co-leading studios integrating current practice methods and digital technologies, with a strong emphasis on collaboration, human-centered and evidence-based design and innovation. 522185 Manhattan 3670015040 Department of Design Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Jan 5 2027 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Interior Design program at Kansas State University invites applications for a 9-month faculty position beginning August 2027. The successful candidate may be appointed as either a tenure-track Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice, depending on qualifications and professional experience. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Our program is distinguished by the scholarly and professional expertise of its faculty and a shared commitment to preparing entry-level interior design professionals. Our curriculum emphasizes collaboration, human-centered and evidence-based design, technical competency, and design approaches that promote health, well-being, and responsible professional practice. We seek a collaborative, future-oriented colleague who brings creative energy, professional expertise, and a commitment to interior design education. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to contribute to a team-based teaching environment and to integrate contemporary professional practice into the curriculum. SHARED TEACHING RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will teach design studios and other courses across the Interior Design curriculum. Candidates should be prepared to integrate contemporary methods and technologies into studio instruction and demonstrate proficiency with software commonly used in professional practice, including Revit, Enscape, and Adobe Creative Cloud. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to teach in design studios and in two or more of the following curricular areas: evidence-based design; history and theory of interior design; materials and construction; textiles; construction documents; building systems and technology; and digital visualization. Studio courses are commonly co-taught. Candidates should therefore demonstrate collaborative professional and/or teaching experience and an ability to contribute effectively to shared course leadership, curriculum coordination, and student learning. APPOINTMENT PATHWAYS TENURE-TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR The tenure-track appointment supports the university's integrated mission of teaching, research/creative scholarship, and service. Teaching \u2014 65\u201370% Teach undergraduate interior design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate's expertise and program needs. Contribute to collaborative teaching, curriculum development, and continuous improvement of the Interior Design program. Research and Creative Scholarship \u2014 25\u201330% Develop and sustain a focused program of research and/or creative scholarship informed by the candidate's academic preparation, professional expertise, teaching interests, or emerging areas of inquiry. The successful candidate's scholarly and creative work will contribute to advancement within the discipline and form an important basis for tenure and promotion. Service \u2014 5\u201310% Contribute to departmental governance; college and university committees and initiatives; student, professional, and community engagement; and relevant disciplinary or professional organizations. PROFESSOR OF PRACTICE The Professor of Practice appointment emphasizes teaching excellence, professional expertise, and engagement with the Interior Design program and profession. Teaching \u2014 80\u201390% Teach undergraduate interior design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate's professional expertise and program needs. Bring substantial professional practice experience into the classroom and contribute to collaborative teaching, curriculum development, and the integration of current professional standards, technologies, and methods. Service \u2014 10\u201320% Contribute to departmental governance, program and college initiatives, student engagement, and professional communities. The successful candidate will help strengthen connections among the program, alumni, practitioners, and the broader interior design profession. About Us The Interior Design program at Kansas State University offers a four-year, first-professional Bachelor of Science in Interior Design. The program is part of the Department of Interior Architecture and Industrial Design (IAID) within the College of Architecture, Planning and Design (APDesign). In 2025, Interior Design celebrated 100 years of design education at Kansas State University. The program enrolls approximately 137 students and is supported by five full-time faculty. It is accredited by the Council for Interior Design Accreditation (CIDA), and Kansas State University is an accredited institutional member of the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD). Our students have earned recognition through national and international design competitions and are valued by employers for their professional preparation, collaborative abilities, and workplace readiness. The 2025 graduating class achieved 100% employment in the field by January 1, 2026. As part of APDesign, Interior Design faculty and students have opportunities to collaborate with programs in Interior Architecture, Industrial Design, Architecture, Landscape Architecture, and Regional & Community Planning. APDesign is housed in the Seaton and Regnier Hall complex, which provides contemporary teaching, research, and collaborative spaces and approximately 20,000 square feet of fabrication and research laboratories. The Interior Design faculty approach design education as a collaborative endeavor. Faculty co-teach studios, coordinate learning across the curriculum, and continually evaluate courses and pedagogical approaches to respond to changes in professional practice, technology, research, and societal needs. We seek a colleague who will contribute to this culture while bringing new perspectives and expertise to the program. Our curriculum prepares interior designers to address complex human and societal needs through evidence-based, human-centered design while meeting professional responsibilities and client expectations. We value intellectual diversity, collaboration, innovation, ethical professional practice, and the role of design in supporting human health and well-being. Additional information may be found at www.ksu.edu (university), apdesign.k-state.edu (college),apdesign.k-state.edu/IAID (department), and www.manhattan.org (community). Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: FOR TENURE-TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR Master's degree or higher in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, or a closely related field. Minimum of three years of professional practice experience in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field and qualified for NCIDQ examination. Demonstrated excellence in written, oral, and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. Demonstrated proficiency with contemporary digital design and visualization tools used in professional practice, including Revit and Adobe Creative Cloud, with experience in Enscape, AutoCAD, and/or comparable platforms. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in collaborative professional and/or teaching environments. Demonstrated potential to establish and sustain a scholarly and/or creative agenda related to the candidate's academic preparation, professional expertise, or areas of design inquiry. FOR PROFESSOR OF PRACTICE Bachelor's degree or higher in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, or a closely related field. Minimum of 10 years of professional practice experience in interior design, interior architecture, architecture, or a closely related field. Current NCIDQ certification. Demonstrated record of professional accomplishment and leadership appropriate to a practice-based faculty appointment. Demonstrated excellence in written, oral, and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. Demonstrated proficiency with contemporary digital design and visualization tools used in professional practice, including Revit and Adobe Creative Cloud, with experience in Enscape, AutoCAD, and/or comparable platforms. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in collaborative professional and/or teaching environments. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: FOR TENURE-TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR PhD or other terminal degree in Interior Design or a related field. More than three years of professional practice experience. NCIDQ certification and/or architectural licensure. Professional certifications or credentials relevant to the discipline, such as WELL, EDAC, LEED, or NKBA credentials. Experience teaching undergraduate design studios, including collaborative or co-teaching environments. Ability to develop and teach courses in multiple areas of the required interior design curriculum. Evidence of an emerging or established record of research, scholarship, and/or creative activity. Record of service to academic and/or professional communities. FOR PROFESSOR OF PRACTICE 15 or more years of professional practice experience. Master's degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, or a closely related field. Architectural licensure and/or additional professional certifications relevant to the discipline, such as WELL, EDAC, LEED, or NKBA credentials. Evidence of leadership in project delivery, design practice, firm leadership, or other areas relevant to interior design education. Previous teaching, mentoring, professional training, or studio instruction experience. Demonstrated ability to teach multiple levels of undergraduate design studio and contribute to co-teaching leadership. Ability to develop and teach courses in multiple areas of the required interior design curriculum. Record of leadership or service within professional organizations and/or the broader design community. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of interest addressing qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Professional portfolio. Teaching portfolio (if taught previously). List of three academic and/or professional references with full contact information. Application Window Applications close on: January 5, 2027 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,000-$78,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c71f9b4e Last Name (required) 89ecfe94 Email (required) 32729122 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: c0d78f94 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education / Instructional Education / Instructional Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 92dec005 Last Name (required) a9e77437 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 95784cf8 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 659e00b1 Last Name (required) 4bdc5a29 Email (required) e573aaf7 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 438c1088 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 6b283ea6 Last Name (required) 46106b6d Email (required) 65f7d37b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 2c1cb11a Last Name (required) df650a49 Email (required) 5a83b1b9 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/seed-equipment-technician-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Seed Equipment Technician", "description": "Seed Equipment Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Seed Equipment Technician - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Seed Equipment Technician Apply Now Seed Equipment Technician The Agricultural Tech II will serve the Foundation Seed Program within the Agronomy Department at Kansas State University. 522405 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Agronomy Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This role serves the Foundation Seed Program within the Agronomy Department at Kansas State University. Reports to the Program Administrator of the Foundation Seed Program with input from Kansas State University breeders of Canola, Soybeans, and Wheat. About Us Here at the Department of Agronomy, we strive to equip students and industry members with the tools they need to serve our communities and society as a whole through agriculture. Through each facet of our work, we emphasize the importance of sustainable and efficient practices to conserve our resources and protect the land. The Kansas Foundation Seed Project has the responsibility for providing the Kansas seed industry with foundation seed of public varieties. The varieties involved include those originated by the Kansas Agricultural Experiment Station and may include varieties developed by other state experiment stations. The crops handled in the project include wheat, soybeans, and canola. The Kansas Foundation Seed Project retail seed sales are limited to seed of the foundation class. Since its inception in 1954, the Kansas Foundation Seed Project has sought to maximize production of outstanding varieties and to make this seed available to seed growers state wide. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: \u2022 High School diploma and one year of relevant experience. \u2022 Experience in operating farm equipment including grain trucks and other specialized equipment. \u2022 Must have skills pertaining to mechanical, electrical, basic woodworking, basic welding, and basic plumbing projects and repairs. \u2022 Driver's license required. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience in the operation of seed conditioning, treating, bagging equipment, and general seed production knowledge. \u2022 Computer skills including experience in Microsoft Word and Excel, and QuickBooks or the ability to learn. \u2022 A Kansas Commercial Pesticide Applicators license in Seed Treatment (4) and Stored Products (7B) categories or the ability to obtain within 6 months, and a Kansas Commercial Driver\u2019s License (CDL) class A or the ability to obtain one within 6 months. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Letter of interest Resume or CV Name, email, and phone number for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $21.63 - $26.44 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) aa1fece2 Last Name (required) c7707b6a Email (required) d3d5bdb7 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: ea00bde9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Agronomy Crop Production Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Agriculture Agronomy Crop Production Plant Sciences Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 9dd57ea5 Last Name (required) 8e1e7782 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 03d4d325 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) cccb437f Last Name (required) 8055793a Email (required) ecb46287 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 898f75ba Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Are