policies. Responsible for the development and review of electronic proposals to Federal agencies and other sponsors as prescribed by the particular agency. About Us The Office of Sponsored Programs provides a one-office approach to the full life cycle of research administration in assisting faculty, staff, and administrators in obtaining and administering funding from non-university sources to support K-State's creative and scholarly activities. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid eligible: This position is eligible for a hybrid work schedule following successful completion of the required training period. Employees are expected to work on-site during training before transitioning to the hybrid schedule. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) Five years of relevant experience Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Three years experience, specifically in Grants and Contract Administration Advanced degree, such as a M.B.A., emphasis on accounting or finance. Certified Research Administrator certification Strong communication (both oral and written) Interpersonal skills experience Experience in the interpretation and application of guidelines, statutes and regulations. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $47,486 - $60,541 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f57e992d Last Name (required) 435f7aba Email (required) 5b856f87 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: b1e35838 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 472ac590 Last Name (required) 0d9343be Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later f79dd2fb Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) b3f0f367 Last Name (required) 1a4dbdc8 Email (required) 3a5a7e4f Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job ebbd4d85 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque 