de dishes using standardized menus and recipes. Assist in the coordination of food production using batch cooking methods. \u2022 Operate, clean, and maintain equipment and work areas in a safe and sanitary manner. Comply with all cleaning and sanitation standards. \u2022 Evaluate HACCP and food safety activities and works closely with others to make sure all equipment and cleaning standards are being met. Store and handle food in a safe and sanitary manner using established procedures. \u2022 Participate as an effective team worker by cooperating with and assisting co-workers and by participating in daily meetings. \u2022 Train and oversee the work of student employees in production area. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, complex, self-operated auxiliary department employing about 1,000 full and part-time staff. As a diverse group, we share the desire to provide exemplary services, products and facilities for our residents and other guests. K-State food has once again landed in the Top 20 nationwide. The Princeton Review's \" The Best 390 Colleges \" has ranked K-State's campus food at No. 14 in its 2025 issue. It's pretty rare for campus meals to be made from scratch on location, and our students appreciate that! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience in commercial/institutional cooking. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to learn to perform basic math computations to accurately weigh and measure ingredients Ability to use and care for equipment Ability to handle food safely while preparing high quality products. Considerable knowledge of large scale food preparation, equipment, health sanitation, and safety procedures. One to three years experience in an institutional or volume setting. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: on-line application Application Window Applications close on: October 30, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $16.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) e5522d5d Last Name (required) a35e2e32 Email (required) 541aaaea Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 94a53500 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Dining / Hospitality Food Safety / Science / Systems Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 6c8bc8ff Last Name (required) 804436a4 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later e352b805 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) ef34feb9 Last Name (required) fe27dc36 Email (required) 58c353dc Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job cc2a9afa Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm L