, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 17909191 Last Name (required) 6556902a Email (required) 2070c264 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 8165ec3b Last Name (required) 22b756a6 Email (required) c55fabe4 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/maintenance-and-repair-tech-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-83506c32-cf2a-48e0-9d02-704079152b16": {"title": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II", "description": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Maintenance and Repair Tech II Apply Now Maintenance and Repair Tech II Maintenance & Repair Tech II responsible for diagnosing, repairing, and maintaining plumbing, electrical, fire safety, building systems, equipment, and facilities while providing excellent customer service. 522168 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Maintenance and Repair Technician II position provides an opportunity to apply your general maintenance and repair expertise in the Jardine Apartments community. This is a full-time position with a consistent work schedule and a generous benefits package. If you take pride in your work, are dependable and conscientious, and are committed to quality workmanship and exceptional customer service, we invite you to consider joining our Housing and Dining Services (HDS) team. Duties and responsibilities include: Diagnose, service, and maintain plumbing and electrical systems and equipment. Test and maintain fire alarm and emergency lighting systems. Independently troubleshoot, maintain, and repair specialized equipment and building systems. Inspect and evaluate fire and life-safety systems to ensure proper operation and identify potential repair needs. Evaluate facilities for pest control needs. Repair and service building hardware and custodial equipment, as well as perform minor furniture repairs and adjustments. Collaborate with departmental staff to maintain and repair facilities and equipment. Provide an exemplary level of customer service to residents, staff, and other members of the university community. Maintain accurate records of work performed and equipment serviced. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, self-operated auxiliary department serving more than 5,000 students that call the K-State campus home. This \"home away from home\" meets more than the basic needs of students living with us \u2014 we provide affordable, safe and engaging accommodations and services for our residents, while finding unique ways to support them in their academic pursuits. We pride ourselves on taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. YOU can help make our residents and guests feel welcome and comfortable! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience. Various training and/or certification may be required. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: High school graduation/GED Journeyman level experience in plumbing, electrical, HVAC Strong troubleshooting skills Ability to read blueprints and schematics Effective oral and written communication skills Knowledge of codes, hazards and safety precautions Ability to consistently demonstrate professionalism and a desire to provide exceptional customer service Ability to effectively interact with others when providing services Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: on-line application Application Window Applications close on: October 30, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.00-$20.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) cb77a908 Last Name (required) 51209a32 Email (required) e6e5bc0f Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d9b38f9f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 135800d0 Last Name (required) cc4779c6 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later e28ed50c Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 64d279e2 Last Name (required) d78a3f1f Email (required) 91250eb9 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 459621ce Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps 