nly\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-associate-full-professor-beef-production-medicine-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor \u2013 Beef Production Medicine", "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor \u2013 Beef Production Medicine - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor \u2013 Beef Production Medicine - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor \u2013 Beef Production Medicine Apply Now Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor \u2013 Beef Production Medicine This position will serve as a member of an active teaching and research faculty team with an emphasis on beef cattle medicine and management that includes teaching in the DVM and Graduate programs, research focused on cattle health and well-being and service that includes continuing education for practicing veterinarians and serving as a subject matter expert for producers. 520666 Manhattan Clinical Sciences Academic / Faculty - 12 month Closing at: Jan 15 2027 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The successful candidate will join an active teaching and research team consisting of several faculty members with an emphasis on beef cattle medicine and management. The ideal candidate will develop a successful beef cattle research program focusing on cattle health, well-being, and production. The successful candidate will be expected to provide teaching related to beef and cattle health management. Teaching activities will include didactic lectures, small group discussions, and laboratories for instruction of veterinary and CVM graduate students. Delivery of continuing education for practicing veterinarians and serving as a content expert for producers are expectations for the position. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Clinical/Assistant Professor: DVM or Equivalent Degree Clinical/Associate Professor: DVM and demonstrate excellence in clinical service, Patient care and clinical instruction Clinical/Full Professor: DVM or Equivalent Degree and demonstrates sustained excellence in clinical service and dedication to continued professional development The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: Relevant advanced training, advanced academic degree, specialty status in a relevant discipline, and/or 5 years of experience in a food animal practice setting. Practice background and clinical experience in beef cattle production medicine Sponsorship eligibility: This position is eligible for sponsorship. Application Window Applications close on: January 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Commensurate with experience. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c0837fb7 Last Name (required) 3b11027b Email (required) 6bbc6f73 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: b1716887 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 12 month Academic / Faculty - 12 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 4f172cff Last Name (required) f0159783 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 5739f989 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) f463ec2b Last Name (required) ac31a026 Email (required) f4d98fe4 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 7c8238a8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job\u2019s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate\u2019s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State\u2019s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 78f0a18e Last Name (required) 0b491c26 Email (required) e6e675d0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) aa14356b Last Name (required) 5952452f Email (required) 4547b246 Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"}, "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/regional-admissions-coordinator-dallas-fort-worth-other-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Regional Admissions Coordinator Dallas/Fort Worth", "description": "Regional Admissions Coordinator Dallas/Fort Worth - Other, Kansas, United States Regional Admissions Coordinator Dallas/Fort Worth - Other, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Regional Admissions Coordinator Dallas/Fort Worth Apply Now Regional Admissions Coordinator Dallas/Fort Worth Kansas State University is seeking a Regional Admissions Coordinator to serve as the university's primary representative throughout the Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex. 522081 Other, Kansas Recruitment and Admissions Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST Remote required Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Kansas State University is seeking a Regional Admissions Coordinator to serve as the university's primary representative throughout the Dallas/Fort Worth metroplex. Working from a DFW-based home office , this position offers the opportunity to build meaningful relationships with prospective undergraduate students while helping them discover how K-State can support their educational, career, and personal goals. The coordinator also cultivates partnerships with high school counselors, educators, community organizations, and other key stakeholders who influence college-going decisions, serving as a trusted resource for students and families throughout their college search journey. The Regional Admissions Coordinator develops and executes a comprehensive territory recruitment strategy designed to attract, engage, and enroll undergraduate students across the Dallas/Fort Worth and North Texas region. This position is responsible for managing a recruitment territory by conducting school visits, attending college fairs and recruitment events, engaging with the Dallas/Fort Worth Admissions Regional Network (DARN), communicating with prospective and admitted students, and providing personalized guidance that helps students navigate key decisions on their path to enrollment. This position requires a high degree of independence, initiative, and territorial ownership. The Regional Admissions Coordinator continuously assesses market opportunities, recruitment performance, and enrollment trends to inform local strategies that increase K-State's visibility and enrollment outcomes throughout the region. Success in the role depends on strong communication skills, strategic thinking, relationship-building abilities, and a commitment to delivering exceptional service to students, families, and educational partners. Working collaboratively with colleagues across the Office of Recruitment and Admissions and university partners, the Regional Admissions Coordinator plays a vital role in advancing enrollment goals and strengthening K-State's presence throughout North Texas. Through each conversation, presentation, school visit, and recruitment event, the coordinator helps future Wildcats envision themselves as members of the K-State community. About Us The Office of Recruitment and Admissions (ORA) serves as the front door to Kansas State University. Our team is committed to building meaningful connections, providing personalized guidance, and creating opportunities for students to discover how K-State can help them achieve their academic, professional, and personal goals. ORA professionals and student staff members, work collaboratively to support students from their first introduction to K-State through enrollment, serving as trusted resources throughout the college search process. Through strategic outreach, relationship building, and student-centered service, our team plays a critical role in shaping the future of the university and helping students find a community to call home. Why Join Our Team This position offers the opportunity to own and grow one of Kansas State University's out-of-state recruitment markets. Successful candidates will have the chance to build lasting relationships with students, families, educators, community partners, and alumni while serving as K-State's primary representative throughout the Dallas/Fort Worth region. The role combines strategic planning, relationship development, public speaking, event management, communication, and student mentorship in an autonomous environment. Each day presents opportunities to connect students with educational opportunities, help families navigate the college search process, and contribute directly to the university's enrollment goals. For professionals who enjoy relationship-building, working independently, traveling throughout their territory, and helping students achieve their goals, this position offers a unique opportunity to make a meaningful impact on both individual students and the future of Kansas State University. Worksite Description This position is remote required, and the individual in position must reside and maintain a home office in the Dallas/Fort Worth metro area . This position is tasked with coordinating an independently developed recruitment strategy for prospective and admitted students (freshmen and transfer) within their territory, including travel throughout the metro area. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a bachelor's degree. Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager. The degree requirement ensures candidates possess advanced first-hand experience in higher education, communication skills and a systems-level understanding of enrollment processes essential for guiding prospective students, interpreting institutional policies and fostering positive engagement throughout the admissions cycle. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and structured learning experiences inherent in a formal bachelor's degree program. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, excellent organization skills, and the ability to work both autonomously and in a team environment. Strong social and Communication skills and the ability to engage with other of a wide array of experiences and backgrounds Comfort in planning and conducting extensive travel independently including, evenings and weekends Possess a high energy level and be able to work under strict deadlines Self-motivation, a team attitude, and a consistent commitment to a high standard of excellence are preferred Demonstrated proficiency with technology and multiple computer programs (i.e Microsoft Office including Knowledge of Excel, customer relationship manager software), and efficient use of e-mail Additional Role Information: Valid driver's license with no restrictions and ability to drive required upon employment Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 9th, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $52000-$55000 with geographic differential for the DFW area for total comp package of $55,000-$58,500 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 6bfa0036 Last Name (required) be28cda6 Email (required) fbf1cc4f Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 8f055807 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Student Affairs / Services Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Student Affairs / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Other, Kansas, United States Other, Kansas, United States Worksite Remote required Remote required Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) bb1ebf32 Last Name (required) f8bccb84 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later ad56bf62 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 3ef1afd7 Last Name (required) c16d287c Email (required) 58554099 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 94516c10 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist 